('When this sad war is over we will all return to our homes, and feel that we can ask no higher honor than the proud consciousness that we belonged to the Army of the Potomac.','George B. McClellan',ARRAY['sad']::text[],'381bf13d2473fde90ad36c83fa08e83f1e8d15f6'),
('In my ballets, woman is first. Men are consorts. God made men to sing the praises of women. They are not equal to men: They are better.','George Balanchine',ARRAY['women']::text[],'5d9dc261dfc664c1a7045ca38f66e728cbdbcb4d'),
('Dishonesty is so grasping it would deceive God himself, were it possible.','George Bancroft',ARRAY['god']::text[],'b1b50f7a3b12810430ce45107f3990fd6c692cfa'),
