('Take all that is given whether wealth, love or language, nothing comes by mistake and with good digestion all can be turned to health.','George Herbert',ARRAY['health']::text[],'d6fe6523c5b1d742ba2439a36fb4868368472335'),
('There would be no great men if there were no little ones.','George Herbert',ARRAY['men']::text[],'a5c1ea2ecc8ad144a9b79f26ee09dc1d16697d6d'),
('A man of great memory without learning hath a rock and a spindle and no staff to spin.','George Herbert',ARRAY['learning']::text[],'83be5721e7819bd7d2eb5fcafd72f9203afe454c'),
('He didn''t want to tell his son what to do, but told me to write the president a letter. I didn''t name a country, but there are many countries we have a fragile relationship with.','George Herbert Walker',ARRAY['relationship']::text[],'4b77a8ddc320043ed103f15278b861cddb04e62b'),
('It''s good to have money and the things that money can buy, but it''s good, too, to check up once in a while and make sure that you haven''t lost the things that money can''t buy.','George Horace Lorimer',ARRAY['money']::text[],'cfd5faf193cfb9d318ec68eb0cd89e465e249ddb'),
('You''ve got to get up every morning with determination if you''re going to go to bed with satisfaction.','George Horace Lorimer',ARRAY['morning']::text[],'249e1a6762db553d990e12cbbb18927a2f23556a'),
('Was there ever such stuff as great as part of Shakespeare? Only one must not say so! But what think you? - What? - Is there not sad stuff? What? - What?','George III',ARRAY['sad']::text[],'0af5e204d78a27e51649f495167c98a98d2a18d5'),
('I spent two years in the Army. And my older brother, who was also a great positive influence on me, encouraged me to think about law school, and I said - well, I didn''t have any money.','George J. Mitchell',ARRAY['positive']::text[],'cd2d3a49d88cd5db4a34920e1e46622643e925d6'),
('I had a great interest in sports. I had three older brothers who were great athletes. I was not.','George J. Mitchell',ARRAY['sports']::text[],'96c30914de34d48949a372d97c4fb5e211bdba87'),
('As they say, one thing led to another, and, ultimately, the British and Irish governments asked me to serve as chairman of the peace negotiations, which ironically began six years ago this week.','George J. Mitchell',ARRAY['peace']::text[],'1b271ac836942b011159d2989c2c874fc31445dc'),
('I really owe everything to my parents and their devotion and drive to see to it that their children had the education which led to the opportunities that they never were able to have.','George J. Mitchell',ARRAY['education']::text[],'e2fcca08a0ec706ce85931d99bc06b941fd728d6'),
('I had been involved in U.S. intelligence in Berlin, Germany, while in the military and had worked with a contact with the Central Intelligence Agency office there.','George J. Mitchell',ARRAY['intelligence']::text[],'ec153c11c81560db7e82ca92bb5b374ac85fc0b8'),
('When I went to college, my goal was to be a college history teacher. I majored in history.','George J. Mitchell',ARRAY['teacher']::text[],'8305e05d9154d7e44b4bc712ab96d5c35b6df231'),
('The result was, of course, that today, tragically, more than 40 million Americans don''t have health insurance, and for many, not having health insurance means they don''t have access to good health care.','George J. Mitchell',ARRAY['health']::text[],'97cefca4f95553df35580cb89a0ae02a92b59252'),
('Love demands infinitely less than friendship.','George Jean Nathan',ARRAY['friendship']::text[],'fe098ff6a00f8aa0476b10a05a3fdfa451653aaf'),
('Love is an emotion experienced by the many and enjoyed by the few.','George Jean Nathan',ARRAY['love']::text[],'135deba51ae9e6c47c7329ccf10da46e8bb95c06'),
('No man can think clearly when his fists are clenched.','George Jean Nathan',ARRAY['anger']::text[],'9cb8676ac112f26b9065dcdd9981d682bab9e6df'),
('To speak of morals in art is to speak of legislature in sex. Art is the sex of the imagination.','George Jean Nathan',ARRAY['art','imagination']::text[],'083481ddbc1e7c8dfba909e711667282aefdea1b'),
('Beauty makes idiots sad and wise men merry.','George Jean Nathan',ARRAY['beauty','men','sad']::text[],'772feddfd81bd9b4e9accbf3a679fa03ea755b26'),
('I know many married men, I even know a few happily married men, but I don''t know one who wouldn''t fall down the first open coal hole running after the first pretty girl who gave him a wink.','George Jean Nathan',ARRAY['men']::text[],'5c858a240210601759cfa4ad8449791ba2c87dec'),
('Criticism is the windows and chandeliers of art: it illuminates the enveloping darkness in which art might otherwise rest only vaguely discernible, and perhaps altogether unseen.','George Jean Nathan',ARRAY['art']::text[],'a4408f8760bd191704137f10191b026f0b6e4d10'),
('Criticism is the art of appraising others at one''s own value.','George Jean Nathan',ARRAY['art']::text[],'0c8b8238ffbec8301fb04bed0df050a5f1df3acf'),
('Patriotism is often an arbitrary veneration of real estate above principles.','George Jean Nathan',ARRAY['patriotism']::text[],'3cfd8844ad6aea7eaf0f98b99d24361de7011989'),
('A man reserves his true and deepest love not for the species of woman in whose company he finds himself electrified and enkindled, but for that one in whose company he may feel tenderly drowsy.','George Jean Nathan',ARRAY['love']::text[],'8d9e460e8d121927880452ef72f73e3001d6743e'),
('Bad officials are the ones elected by good citizens who do not vote.','George Jean Nathan',ARRAY['good']::text[],'51a53e7fefb205ee5a79845a88ccc07edd73d2a9'),
('Women, as they grow older, rely more and more on cosmetics. Men, as they grow older, rely more and more on a sense of humor.','George Jean Nathan',ARRAY['humor','men','women']::text[],'0c02eb9890ae2c521df50f593a01f50897b9c7fd'),
('It is only the cynicism that is born of success that is penetrating and valid.','George Jean Nathan',ARRAY['success']::text[],'ab0914e64d8a264d823c7028c947a57a4abddfd7'),
('Politics is the diversion of trivial men who, when they succeed at it, become important in the eyes of more trivial men.','George Jean Nathan',ARRAY['politics']::text[],'2c09fb4c6ab6b0c5b66405462fb49d1c07856763'),
('Great art is as irrational as great music. It is mad with its own loveliness.','George Jean Nathan',ARRAY['art','great','music']::text[],'f1a31fac7ed9dee04f42317594021cc63ee9d7f4'),
('Country fans need to support country music by buying albums and concert tickets for traditional artists or the music will just fade away. And that would be really sad.','George Jones',ARRAY['music','sad']::text[],'f4684d2cef95eccafcf21253269dc08767781d15'),
('The architecture of our future is not only unfinished the scaffolding has hardly gone up.','George Lamming',ARRAY['architecture']::text[],'c9b242d74a5ce8695ef56c139d34caccdc6fa62f'),
('Competition is the spice of sports but if you make spice the whole meal you''ll be sick.','George Leonard',ARRAY['sports']::text[],'6721ac3601cf8858c124bd60f9e23836f690eff5'),
('We march and fight, to death or on to victory. Our might is right, no traitors shall prevail. Our hearts are steeled against the fiery gates of hell. No shot or shell, can still our mighty song.','George Lincoln Rockwell',ARRAY['death']::text[],'79aa3eb26a4c2345f3d18fe774b1e7c602e75b5b'),
('We must make it an imperative duty of our government to protect the gifts which Nature has bestowed on America and to insure the maintenance of a clean, healthy, wholesome environment for our people.','George Lincoln Rockwell',ARRAY['government','nature']::text[],'af68d28ce0039457aa179f16729edeaea1444b7f'),
('Hurried and worried until we''re buried, and there''s no curtain call, Lifes a very funny proposition after all.','George M. Cohan',ARRAY['funny']::text[],'f3b9a9e64a2373c158b51257538ffce2950cb005'),
('You can''t set a hen in one morning and have chicken salad for lunch.','George M. Humphrey',ARRAY['history','morning']::text[],'5a7d6742e9fb5759e34360e8d9881230442b95c3'),
('It''s a terribly hard job to spend a billion dollars and get your money''s worth.','George M. Humphrey',ARRAY['money']::text[],'c214739b1d613db226326a1f169fd24fda567dd6'),
('If instead of a gem, or even a flower, we should cast the gift of a loving thought into the heart of a friend, that would be giving as the angels give.','George MacDonald',ARRAY['friendship']::text[],'00da351946ac525e0c3d9fa43fc24650508a9b77'),
('To have what we want is riches but to be able to do without is power.','George MacDonald',ARRAY['power']::text[],'db29605f3c3fd14fff98ff6e453197f44d99d4ee'),
('Man finds it hard to get what he wants, because he does not want the best God finds it hard to give, because He would give the best, and man will not take it.','George MacDonald',ARRAY['best','god']::text[],'521858e51fb593ddd3e63ece05c3b68d6ae56c9e'),
('To be trusted is a greater compliment than being loved.','George MacDonald',ARRAY['trust']::text[],'35e25d7185b754645cb87edb19a3d0882dc040dc'),
('It is our best work that God wants, not the dregs of our exhaustion. I think he must prefer quality to quantity.','George MacDonald',ARRAY['best','god','work']::text[],'6d0e41286ceed4229c363d7254b2d36fb8b95acf'),
('When we are out of sympathy with the young, then I think our work in this world is over.','George MacDonald',ARRAY['sympathy']::text[],'cdc18f8baef3c6b5d6232bd3326e2205556f6962'),
('Forgiveness is the giving, and so the receiving, of life.','George MacDonald',ARRAY['forgiveness']::text[],'73a0b63ba415526ebb46820e868a114addfd198a'),
('Age is not all decay it is the ripening, the swelling, of the fresh life within, that withers and bursts the husk.','George MacDonald',ARRAY['age']::text[],'88db4700aeb9ede924f042968f32951b7dde0bf1'),
('Few delights can equal the presence of one whom we trust utterly.','George MacDonald',ARRAY['trust']::text[],'15f1c93f01c2c1a40238811f01010a4779360bff'),
('How strange this fear of death is! We are never frightened at a sunset.','George MacDonald',ARRAY['death','fear']::text[],'1d5c5db6369e4e9a04ccb3e964d2bca980fe595f'),
('The best preparation for the future is the present well seen to, and the last duty done.','George MacDonald',ARRAY['future']::text[],'580576d63753440895e2500460b06c9470dc722f'),
('Attitudes are more important than facts.','George MacDonald',ARRAY['attitude']::text[],'3704cf7fa4526e6bc1666b9c109bca94853d6a45'),
('The principle part of faith is patience.','George MacDonald',ARRAY['faith','patience']::text[],'49fe9afca1aa8fc59365515397d6dbb41b55aa7f'),
('It is not in the nature of politics that the best men should be elected. The best men do not want to govern their fellowmen.','George MacDonald',ARRAY['best','men','nature','politics']::text[],'fe63532fc05ef1f0466136b5787b1704c212eb24'),
('In all our associations in all our agreements let us never lose sight of this fundamental maxim - that all power was originally lodged in, and consequently is derived from, the people.','George Mason',ARRAY['power']::text[],'3921e6718b84e6b050cbd9b8f8e8fb424d0bd928'),
('Your dear baby has died innocent and blameless, and has been called away by an all wise and merciful Creator, most probably from a life to misery and misfortune, and most certainly to one of happiness and bliss.','George Mason',ARRAY['happiness']::text[],'65c8e71f82cdf2b4fcada6b3933be462a8bc1476'),
('A few years'' experience will convince us that those things which at the time they happened we regarded as our greatest misfortunes have proved our greatest blessings.','George Mason',ARRAY['experience','time']::text[],'e7c40b9498087a49539a974f3515bde42123505a'),
('Every society, all government, and every kind of civil compact therefore, is or ought to be, calculated for the general good and safety of the community.','George Mason',ARRAY['society']::text[],'da3040f889aca9a3733434df9ec5dc011d180265'),
('It is not patriotic to commit young Americans to war unless our national security clearly requires it.','George McGovern',ARRAY['war']::text[],'9340911d02d78b73837b38dfe25a088c509fdebe'),
('Politics is an act of faith you have to show some kind of confidence in the intellectual and moral capacity of the public.','George McGovern',ARRAY['faith','politics']::text[],'1f7d08dfdf6d3d3cedf45c173c347097bb27f6fb'),
('I think the country''s getting disgusted with Washington partly because of the decline of civility in government.','George McGovern',ARRAY['government']::text[],'d04f5cc122ac95aee50ca48d15284a380b392bf6'),
('I make one pledge above all others - to seek and speak the truth with all the resources of mind and spirit I command.','George McGovern',ARRAY['truth']::text[],'04736eba831f484e721e856be0064e45e872fb15'),
('It''s a tough thing, to know what to do about a war that deep in your gut you feel is wrong and yet watch your peers going off to fight in that war.','George McGovern',ARRAY['war']::text[],'8c81498bd9f2f9379eef89484000de1e17ff1cd3'),
('I did frequently refer to my war record in World War II, but not in any flamboyant way.','George McGovern',ARRAY['war']::text[],'1f62f9f5b08e217299d7904f5c18dc31801a4716'),
('When I was in the war, I was lucky that I was in a plane and never saw the carnage close-up.','George McGovern',ARRAY['war']::text[],'305524d88c8602b4b9dc6e21b1f78730c4e4916d'),
('I''ve come to realize that protecting freedom of choice in our everyday lives is essential to maintaining a healthy civil society.','George McGovern',ARRAY['freedom','society']::text[],'59df4fc2f83a0533395c08bffca2f968642de3fb'),
('Democrats believe that the federal government is not our enemy, it''s our partner.','George McGovern',ARRAY['government']::text[],'7e8060408d23a940f0f8bef58282326502ce963d'),
('The truth is that I oppose the Iraq war, just as I opposed the Vietnam War, because these two conflicts have weakened the U.S. and diminished our standing in the world and our national security.','George McGovern',ARRAY['truth','war']::text[],'cb83bfca3db8abacbb5a06a2d9c6e8ba2ba1d602'),
('I always thought of myself as a moderate liberal, a fighter for peace and justice. I never thought of myself as being all that far out.','George McGovern',ARRAY['peace']::text[],'aa90e4bb7e03d9d1b9247af79802451460fb961b'),
('I was the guy who was constantly speaking out against the Vietnam War. I have no regrets about that.','George McGovern',ARRAY['war']::text[],'22fa0d00a2bf8bbe13169c6fb209daf1b89e9ab1'),
('People didn''t have the political guts to stand up against an American war.','George McGovern',ARRAY['war']::text[],'c1487673938f55cb09854ac97bdea80912b109d9'),
('My dad was a Methodist minister.','George McGovern',ARRAY['dad']::text[],'0c63e8a8302e1eb7ed2b3617eb56b014f3023011'),
('The highest patriotism is not a blind acceptance of official policy, but a love of one''s country deep enough to call her to a higher plain.','George McGovern',ARRAY['love','patriotism']::text[],'470b483789595cfb559bab1ab49b405ee652356f'),
('When I was a youngster growing up in South Dakota, we never referred to the national debt, it was always referred to as the war debt because it stemmed from World War I.','George McGovern',ARRAY['war']::text[],'aacad05e20e02fb2cca8702a5ada810169f4ba33'),
('I hope someday we will be able to proclaim that we have banished hunger in the United States, and that we''ve been able to bring nutrition and health to the whole world.','George McGovern',ARRAY['health','hope']::text[],'71d4010067e1ff088ac5bed6f9d3b4c6a592194e'),
('I hope I live long enough to see every hungry school child in the world being fed under the so-called McGovern-Dole program.','George McGovern',ARRAY['hope']::text[],'c870fd88c803d861306dd36274560a9ebf461e0b'),
('From secrecy and deception in high places, come home, America. From military spending so wasteful that it weakens our nation, come home, America.','George McGovern',ARRAY['home']::text[],'c37cd2c6cbe336ffea3a9fd109c360ffa0653685'),
('The Establishment center... has led us into the stupidest and cruelest war in all history. That war is a moral and political disaster - a terrible cancer eating away at the soul of our nation.','George McGovern',ARRAY['history','war']::text[],'40fcfdf64995b8b54f59b23873c0c189f05f795f'),
('I thought the Vietnam war was an utter, unmitigated disaster, so it was very hard for me to say anything good about it.','George McGovern',ARRAY['war']::text[],'08da4a488f8e1844cb416a0c89376800c105b35f')
INSERT INTO quotes_library (quote, author, tags, quote_hash) VALUES
('I would not plan to base my campaign primarily on opposition to the war in the Persian Gulf.','George McGovern',ARRAY['war']::text[],'2833035c124e62be021f47a687fdef730e037a0f'),
('I think it was my study of history that convinced me that the Democratic Party was more on the side of the average American.','George McGovern',ARRAY['history']::text[],'caa7f56abee4ddd1badec49ebffd314e0fbf5d47'),
('I''m fed up to the ears with old men dreaming up wars for young men to die in.','George McGovern',ARRAY['men','war']::text[],'98143e7bdf8554524f5d0929ee71703311375dd5'),
('There is a strong tendency in the United States to rally round the flag and their troops, no matter how mistaken the war.','George McGovern',ARRAY['war']::text[],'a8d9a00d4f39d903599be93b592b0a3fd329872e'),
('Well, we ought to be stirred, even to tears, by society''s ills.','George McGovern',ARRAY['society']::text[],'d606bdb2276f556125a9bbf232f21e3ee46b12f8'),
('I seek to call America home to those principles that gave us birth.','George McGovern',ARRAY['home']::text[],'7bfd547b6495adcc6aca5409e99fb0ffd23cbf30'),
('A witty woman is a treasure a witty beauty is a power.','George Meredith',ARRAY['beauty','power']::text[],'381fe1b742aab242774e003e5e54fdd009e59ef6'),
('Jealousy is love bed of burning snarl.','George Meredith',ARRAY['jealousy']::text[],'a602f9f8326a4d99e52bbbf67195bd735c4c0394'),
('The man of science is nothing if not a poet gone wrong.','George Meredith',ARRAY['science']::text[],'dc6676d9d2ee48514d96b58ffb680fa5796fa6d5'),
('The most dire disaster in love is the death of imagination.','George Meredith',ARRAY['death','imagination']::text[],'92acbeb00620eae066fd11aff022d007fee1dfd6'),
('In England only uneducated people show off their knowledge nobody quotes Latin or Greek authors in the course of conversation, unless he has never read them.','George Mikes',ARRAY['knowledge']::text[],'7e16503f49dc04f9b446b5c9bb7f9189856e4ba7'),
('On the Continent people have good food in England people have good table manners.','George Mikes',ARRAY['food','good']::text[],'01e523d7a80a9a21cd103b4db5a7a65d7f498efe'),
('The first question at that time in poetry was simply the question of honesty, of sincerity.','George Oppen',ARRAY['poetry']::text[],'eedf993160dcff48b640b50cfde0f54e32f69656'),
('Clarity, clarity, surely clarity is the most beautiful thing in the world, A limited, limiting clarity I have not and never did have any motive of poetry But to achieve clarity.','George Oppen',ARRAY['poetry']::text[],'174af55e339652bfe850717686e9613423da22b0'),
('The intellectual is different from the ordinary man, but only in certain sections of his personality, and even then not all the time.','George Orwell',ARRAY['time']::text[],'2eb9c44cb016a898ed6977dc6392f6fccb018771'),
('People sleep peaceably in their beds at night only because rough men stand ready to do violence on their behalf.','George Orwell',ARRAY['men']::text[],'650edd6455d606b2aef84a1c0a828a5d9ca698e1'),
('For a creative writer possession of the ''truth'' is less important than emotional sincerity.','George Orwell',ARRAY['truth']::text[],'cfed38e3ea3fc105df81ec1d577b0bf11de0e174'),
('Oceania was at war with Eurasia therefore Oceania had always been at war with Eurasia.','George Orwell',ARRAY['war']::text[],'6387abbaf0d712c1b0fbe354bb311c89d6e68e7f'),
('Doublethink means the power of holding two contradictory beliefs in one''s mind simultaneously, and accepting both of them.','George Orwell',ARRAY['power']::text[],'c7f4c2c5005fdd027e4e3604b5e981a28c635122'),
('As with the Christian religion, the worst advertisement for Socialism is its adherents.','George Orwell',ARRAY['religion']::text[],'cec9afce1830a871c571ce1a51cb317def281def'),
('The quickest way of ending a war is to lose it.','George Orwell',ARRAY['war']::text[],'e9e6f05ed274d177037aa1d0d5dabf250442fd5a'),
('Sometimes the first duty of intelligent men is the restatement of the obvious.','George Orwell',ARRAY['men']::text[],'439f841ebd0d0607a362a0a443796fa257455d18'),
('Who controls the past controls the future. Who controls the present controls the past.','George Orwell',ARRAY['future']::text[],'ee636b183a92922c1afde5a50b0ffb49e73eb4d8'),
('He was an embittered atheist, the sort of atheist who does not so much disbelieve in God as personally dislike Him.','George Orwell',ARRAY['god']::text[],'9715915594f69581cc8f2e48a8f58246e3ff44e1'),
('I doubt whether classical education ever has been or can be successfully carried out without corporal punishment.','George Orwell',ARRAY['education']::text[],'fb2395c59908659a6cee6c3873b53de186a9d9d3'),
('We have now sunk to a depth at which restatement of the obvious is the first duty of intelligent men.','George Orwell',ARRAY['intelligence','men']::text[],'7d9aa8a23f48c9e49014f1b0b78940bb98dfcda2'),
('No one can look back on his schooldays and say with truth that they were altogether unhappy.','George Orwell',ARRAY['truth']::text[],'8929a9f70a99b8ef6c4e6ce40fe9088e035455f6'),
('In a time of universal deceit - telling the truth is a revolutionary act.','George Orwell',ARRAY['time','truth']::text[],'49ffeabf9ba40c96747a93ee575cd96ef8960cae'),
('The essential act of war is destruction, not necessarily of human lives, but of the products of human labor.','George Orwell',ARRAY['war']::text[],'0e523fc01d3133e99d531d3c37ee69d78216703c'),
('Mankind is not likely to salvage civilization unless he can evolve a system of good and evil which is independent of heaven and hell.','George Orwell',ARRAY['good']::text[],'a02082b8600ce1754a36221b6c6106830d318ad8'),
('We sleep safe in our beds because rough men stand ready in the night to visit violence on those who would do us harm.','George Orwell',ARRAY['men']::text[],'8b0c33898cbe2a7f7118468bd44f2dc643ae588a'),
('In our time political speech and writing are largely the defense of the indefensible.','George Orwell',ARRAY['time']::text[],'b82a4c5f4d226ff1327358601d45665c0b8c326e'),
('Patriotism is usually stronger than class hatred, and always stronger than internationalism.','George Orwell',ARRAY['patriotism']::text[],'b8a3ebc270216fff9335c4abb248d020d820756c'),
('Good writing is like a windowpane.','George Orwell',ARRAY['good']::text[],'f524e0e3b01fb328ae399b216c3964223ff6272d'),
('We may find in the long run that tinned food is a deadlier weapon than the machine-gun.','George Orwell',ARRAY['food']::text[],'bad2dadf835ee1a844835f31f04a63b41257c541'),
('Happiness can exist only in acceptance.','George Orwell',ARRAY['happiness']::text[],'dffec12473ac7d5a4e05350e75b21309b08d7e6e'),
('Part of the reason for the ugliness of adults, in a child''s eyes, is that the child is usually looking upwards, and few faces are at their best when seen from below.','George Orwell',ARRAY['best']::text[],'f11e3705460729d1f2a6fe9fa3554c5379b25b1d'),
('There are some ideas so wrong that only a very intelligent person could believe in them.','George Orwell',ARRAY['intelligence']::text[],'100407b63dd2c18dc6df76e2caa8e7ba65cfb41c'),
('In our age there is no such thing as ''keeping out of politics.'' All issues are political issues, and politics itself is a mass of lies, evasions, folly, hatred and schizophrenia.','George Orwell',ARRAY['age','politics']::text[],'49191b171133e5685fbf2a1723dc34276f53fd3d'),
('Four legs good, two legs bad.','George Orwell',ARRAY['good']::text[],'3ac7d872b26ff91a94045a5a213842faec829497'),
('War is peace. Freedom is slavery. Ignorance is strength.','George Orwell',ARRAY['freedom','peace','strength','war']::text[],'fd4292cdd29a545671eb16eb4c364805aaf1ae55'),
('Nationalism is power hunger tempered by self-deception.','George Orwell',ARRAY['power']::text[],'e6908531767f176f161c08abffbbfeec9ab80075'),
('If you want a vision of the future, imagine a boot stamping on a human face - forever.','George Orwell',ARRAY['future','imagination']::text[],'49c02b57ad65cbbfae21fda2c70b31c1a01a48c2'),
('On the whole, human beings want to be good, but not too good, and not quite all the time.','George Orwell',ARRAY['good','time']::text[],'aac27b5d8596c8d8ff8b42fd9846327d6ff3e801'),
('War is evil, but it is often the lesser evil.','George Orwell',ARRAY['war']::text[],'576fbc4b3e1c5acba33b54fa128d59e23afee3aa'),
('Society has always seemed to demand a little more from human beings than it will get in practice.','George Orwell',ARRAY['society']::text[],'5f84edf8b0881758aefa2cbb688b62b8001e693b'),
('Freedom is the right to tell people what they do not want to hear.','George Orwell',ARRAY['freedom']::text[],'9e7a68a0539c6303fed679c2734a97e11b89e8a0'),
('To walk through the ruined cities of Germany is to feel an actual doubt about the continuity of civilization.','George Orwell',ARRAY['war']::text[],'57039a989ebb1b0ce4a1a7044702a09391af63e5'),
('No advance in wealth, no softening of manners, no reform or revolution has ever brought human equality a millimeter nearer.','George Orwell',ARRAY['equality']::text[],'fcb35d1fd70919c429612f5fd3b28f16fe327e67'),
('There is hardly such a thing as a war in which it makes no difference who wins. Nearly always one side stands more of less for progress, the other side more or less for reaction.','George Orwell',ARRAY['war']::text[],'1fbe672ed8f0613b5143a4c916f04c2f535277b0'),
('The very concept of objective truth is fading out of the world. Lies will pass into history.','George Orwell',ARRAY['history','truth']::text[],'ce400f16f45e1924ad07a5ab8be7ae576602378c'),
('Power is not a means, it is an end. One does not establish a dictatorship in order to safeguard a revolution one makes the revolution in order to establish the dictatorship.','George Orwell',ARRAY['power']::text[],'97f406c6ff88fba09257f7761e11480a0e284162'),
('Freedom is the freedom to say that two plus two make four. If that is granted, all else follows.','George Orwell',ARRAY['freedom']::text[],'8d0472257ba08c91ef2c0c900e8d5abea0dbdbac'),
('Serious sport has nothing to do with fair play. It is bound up with hatred, jealousy, boastfulness, disregard of all rules and sadistic pleasure in witnessing violence. In other words, it is war minus the shooting.','George Orwell',ARRAY['jealousy','sports','war']::text[],'41317d04968bb55d8f8a66e5af9258ed70aa22b3'),
('Men are only as good as their technical development allows them to be.','George Orwell',ARRAY['good','men']::text[],'6e619883629993cec7ec290a44698c1ccfeec32d'),
('Serious sport is war minus the shooting.','George Orwell',ARRAY['war']::text[],'e353c88d316b4bf54732c9aa828558c3b88bc6c0'),
('War against a foreign country only happens when the moneyed classes think they are going to profit from it.','George Orwell',ARRAY['war']::text[],'768b7f30a2b52c66d715739c238e01f86409bc49'),
('War is war. The only good human being is a dead one.','George Orwell',ARRAY['good','war']::text[],'8d286869f0da7415d9e4da420515a037f59c81e0'),
('Men can only be happy when they do not assume that the object of life is happiness.','George Orwell',ARRAY['happiness','men']::text[],'a1ac2dfec5d604fd82992f3bc8e7049cdc2ab6c3'),
('Every war when it comes, or before it comes, is represented not as a war but as an act of self-defense against a homicidal maniac.','George Orwell',ARRAY['war']::text[],'84136c2d923e99584425c23e7b0cbabc5c7166c8'),
('Not to expose your true feelings to an adult seems to be instinctive from the age of seven or eight onwards.','George Orwell',ARRAY['age']::text[],'2fd74c0a94aacc08bfef2f15527ea5d4511601ab'),
('War is a way of shattering to pieces... materials which might otherwise be used to make the masses too comfortable and... too intelligent.','George Orwell',ARRAY['war']::text[],'69c8aa68253150cd203d04f8e6a951ea76cd159e'),
('Whatever is funny is subversive, every joke is ultimately a custard pie... a dirty joke is a sort of mental rebellion.','George Orwell',ARRAY['funny']::text[],'de01a946705f6b6fd39d4d3fef88249cc066c55d'),
('Liberal: a power worshipper without power.','George Orwell',ARRAY['power']::text[],'9afabfb9821f3db05c4f0ca0983fa3b27b26563d'),
('If you have embraced a creed which appears to be free from the ordinary dirtiness of politics - a creed from which you yourself cannot expect to draw any material advantage - surely that proves that you are in the right?','George Orwell',ARRAY['politics']::text[],'c89848a68e725f3ea4abd3ef9866bcc06140f875'),
('It is also true that one can write nothing readable unless one constantly struggles to efface one''s own personality. Good prose is like a windowpane.','George Orwell',ARRAY['good']::text[],'fdee269fae2d05b3bfda4d000ddacafdc67c3d4f'),
('A family with the wrong members in control that, perhaps, is as near as one can come to describing England in a phrase.','George Orwell',ARRAY['family']::text[],'c3bccb15ebf5f24b472c2e66c1c97439af761c61'),
('The best books... are those that tell you what you know already.','George Orwell',ARRAY['best']::text[],'82b258ebb6918f59b1dc0e1700b23d0a73ed9354'),
('Tonight I should like to thank all those who have shared my work and to acknowledge the debt that I owe to my wife whose encouragement to put research before all other things has been a great strength to me.','George Porter',ARRAY['strength']::text[],'771c21ad1f782869c96f1ac376c59ed1ed0d2095'),
('When the honour is given to that scientist personally the happiness is sweet indeed. Science is, on the whole, an informal activity, a life of shirt sleeves and coffee served in beakers.','George Porter',ARRAY['happiness']::text[],'2e2fce8eb6aac78ab48e58d1c40702d84b1d8738'),
('I have no doubt that we will be successful in harnessing the sun''s energy. If sunbeams were weapons of war, we would have had solar energy centuries ago.','George Porter',ARRAY['war']::text[],'1999573b931411eb7473c24eaf445375bb53622d'),
('Part of it went on gambling, and part of it went on women. The rest I spent foolishly.','George Raft',ARRAY['women']::text[],'df5e3f3d70e70c0b0fb212de8f41f179160a03b6'),
('Under capitalism each individual engages in economic planning.','George Reisman',ARRAY['finance']::text[],'1295dba0564e7571aea0bf167104ebe4dba0ef00'),
('Untutored courage is useless in the face of educated bullets.','George S. Patton',ARRAY['courage']::text[],'d00411d6ef530ddb3aafb9c8ab9eee43a906d61c'),
('If a man does his best, what else is there?','George S. Patton',ARRAY['best']::text[],'bbf231e04fc07a10e81b6a15dbd452a5a9264695'),
('Success is how high you bounce when you hit bottom.','George S. Patton',ARRAY['success']::text[],'372511fa2e30d29a42aa5b3bb1e2edf3849413a7'),
('I don''t measure a man''s success by how high he climbs but how high he bounces when he hits bottom.','George S. Patton',ARRAY['success']::text[],'b4ef85b7133f7bbdcd0020a7ec5e92b85675fa73'),
('Wars may be fought with weapons, but they are won by men. It is the spirit of men who follow and of the man who leads that gains the victory.','George S. Patton',ARRAY['men']::text[],'bd5c310e3fc197c4ccd9241640a1a669ad4fe129'),
('A good plan violently executed now is better than a perfect plan executed next week.','George S. Patton',ARRAY['good']::text[],'98562412ac88b4c69c4414c0c8f8a85dae8e3cc3'),
('You need to overcome the tug of people against you as you reach for high goals.','George S. Patton',ARRAY['motivational']::text[],'af0185b16f94163dccf628c5bbad02c54d94537a'),
('No bastard ever won a war by dying for his country. He won it by making the other poor dumb bastard die for his country.','George S. Patton',ARRAY['war']::text[],'a5592849cae7cd495308715a1c2df4cf6d174b3e'),
('If we take the generally accepted definition of bravery as a quality which knows no fear, I have never seen a brave man. All men are frightened. The more intelligent they are, the more they are frightened.','George S. Patton',ARRAY['fear','men']::text[],'a9d1e039bd29bf11024aeb1946f4c83165b94734'),
('The test of success is not what you do when you are on top. Success is how high you bounce when you hit bottom.','George S. Patton',ARRAY['success']::text[],'6d55bee240ac1b2f805de62f75266088d9e783cc'),
('Prepare for the unknown by studying how others in the past have coped with the unforeseeable and the unpredictable.','George S. Patton',ARRAY['learning']::text[],'be25aaa95b0783413938feef5e3a468d35d73dd5'),
('Americans love to fight. All real Americans love the sting of battle.','George S. Patton',ARRAY['history','love']::text[],'9c7288f65a470f1a68462d92548e1021e6def2dd'),
('Courage is fear holding on a minute longer.','George S. Patton',ARRAY['courage','fear']::text[],'d897964701083211b493b1f0a96026702bc7e622'),
('Never tell people how to do things. Tell them what to do and they will surprise you with their ingenuity.','George S. Patton',ARRAY['wisdom']::text[],'b62e7fc822e819a22220cea036117fa41a18b66e'),
('Americans play to win at all times. I wouldn''t give a hoot and hell for a man who lost and laughed. That''s why Americans have never lost nor ever lose a war.','George S. Patton',ARRAY['war']::text[],'8d25f13502cdc5ab4169cd1a384e9c6d68b1aa04'),
('If you tell people where to go, but not how to get there, you''ll be amazed at the results.','George S. Patton',ARRAY['amazing']::text[],'175b7e387dc19bc8f5a1f779764a3a11a704a93b'),
('If everyone is thinking alike, then somebody isn''t thinking.','George S. Patton',ARRAY['imagination']::text[],'f396ece527e874ec2eb237e1982d0a5d31cd5fc2'),
('A pint of sweat, saves a gallon of blood.','George S. Patton',ARRAY['history']::text[],'475039654da43646ea83b47d9361c00f49ee1a34'),
('The object of war is not to die for your country but to make the other bastard die for his.','George S. Patton',ARRAY['war']::text[],'029d3fa1cbb1ce987a8938cef843e7985b2cfacc'),
('Do your damnedest in an ostentatious manner all the time.','George S. Patton',ARRAY['time']::text[],'95ba0441af81b68227ba4bf48b5108fab9cc0c04'),
('It is foolish and wrong to mourn the men who died. Rather we should thank God that such men lived.','George S. Patton',ARRAY['god','men']::text[],'c302205f01e3322edcc329d65e681c2b50813f58'),
('There is a time to take counsel of your fears, and there is a time to never listen to any fear.','George S. Patton',ARRAY['fear','time']::text[],'5d905ffebabaa358390564075b4da8d3d7e51330'),
('Work is not man''s punishment. It is his reward and his strength and his pleasure.','George Sand',ARRAY['strength','work']::text[],'a1b3feb47f6a43f9885cb1379cf434a7bbe43a3c'),
('Women love always: when earth slips from them, they take refuge in heaven.','George Sand',ARRAY['women']::text[],'dbb1b84fe00ef7dee055961ac0673f19817f1e20'),
('Don''t walk in front of me, I may not follow. Don''t walk behind me, I may not lead. There is only one happiness in life, to love and be loved.','George Sand',ARRAY['happiness','love']::text[],'99f35b0835f2388268ca0633b0b97471678e40ef'),
('Simplicity is the most difficult thing to secure in this world it is the last limit of experience and the last effort of genius.','George Sand',ARRAY['experience']::text[],'b9dc7a7d486e0a239f32452412ef4268d956464a'),
('Life in common among people who love each other is the ideal of happiness.','George Sand',ARRAY['happiness']::text[],'2d1dd4912bb4c2c45c27e74e867d77865ffb14b6'),
('Try to keep your soul young and quivering right up to old age.','George Sand',ARRAY['age']::text[],'9d6f4d9ecc242c667aaa0fab418e82a5e96164ba'),
('The beauty that addresses itself to the eyes is only the spell of the moment the eye of the body is not always that of the soul.','George Sand',ARRAY['beauty']::text[],'96a075daae94c0a33090616cb5ee70ac62e5cd21'),
('He who draws noble delights from sentiments of poetry is a true poet, though he has never written a line in all his life.','George Sand',ARRAY['poetry']::text[],'13c64d8ca4d588029775fcd9f81a4595d5a5967e'),
('There is only one happiness in this life, to love and be loved.','George Sand',ARRAY['happiness','love']::text[],'ebfde27e208da45a1ad3c7b8c77106c5723a9fd4'),
('Never build your emotional life on the weaknesses of others.','George Santayana',ARRAY['life']::text[],'8c95ba15501916a42d452d15bfdd29a43275448f'),
('Wisdom comes by disillusionment.','George Santayana',ARRAY['wisdom']::text[],'4196929ac629b084e9efaaf5126a711df999d5f1'),
