('Truth is the beginning of every good to the gods, and of every good to man.','Plato',ARRAY['good','truth']::text[],'507c455d01f544a90080cefb8bedc796526300de'),
('The punishment which the wise suffer who refuse to take part in the government, is to live under the government of worse men.','Plato',ARRAY['government','men']::text[],'5b4d8c83ba9636759439428724cd3d84e57903bc'),
('Must not all things at the last be swallowed up in death?','Plato',ARRAY['death']::text[],'22b8edab847fce01db9cd9eaa8a2c79d1d3410d9'),
('Then not only an old man, but also a drunkard, becomes a second time a child.','Plato',ARRAY['time']::text[],'7241b0c10f95cb60cc6b163daa89f04aec070025'),
('Then not only custom, but also nature affirms that to do is more disgraceful than to suffer injustice, and that justice is equality.','Plato',ARRAY['equality','nature']::text[],'eb59e9e1d06756dac5727c6e30d5e4d95fcc1960'),
('Good people do not need laws to tell them to act responsibly, while bad people will find a way around the laws.','Plato',ARRAY['good']::text[],'a1c89028a7a27169db2471be535dadc4b9dc3e1b'),
('Whatever deceives men seems to produce a magical enchantment.','Plato',ARRAY['men']::text[],'ab9564c055c36c8ac2213b4a4dbd7273a58de750'),
('Love is a serious mental disease.','Plato',ARRAY['love']::text[],'2046b8ee34dc2116436f575072c2cd8726f6acec'),
('Good actions give strength to ourselves and inspire good actions in others.','Plato',ARRAY['good','strength']::text[],'3120446493b90de1203dc8781965da90afef2b3c'),
('Poetry is nearer to vital truth than history.','Plato',ARRAY['history','poetry','truth']::text[],'696218e7f72a8b8c4796fe8367599291ba8dfe5e'),
('Philosophy is the highest music.','Plato',ARRAY['music']::text[],'0760a1511da3bdc202380ffce42e5b7424dd2648'),
('It is a common saying, and in everybody''s mouth, that life is but a sojourn.','Plato',ARRAY['life']::text[],'adeb22f61855e31e31b566c2f6a03b3c684a2af8'),
('Twice and thrice over, as they say, good is it to repeat and review what is good.','Plato',ARRAY['good']::text[],'72a9e178bf258f9bb3699896dd460b13fe070379'),
('Injustice is censured because the censures are afraid of suffering, and not from any fear which they have of doing injustice.','Plato',ARRAY['fear']::text[],'5011f8775dc9d77865db79a4825e23fa1b502b24'),
('Nothing in the affairs of men is worthy of great anxiety.','Plato',ARRAY['great','men']::text[],'e382ffcfe9fc764033d126b1599f8399331d8beb'),
('Love is the joy of the good, the wonder of the wise, the amazement of the Gods.','Plato',ARRAY['good','love']::text[],'8dbf6fa3ce7c4123620e10ce488b6606e4a9d472'),
('There are three classes of men lovers of wisdom, lovers of honor, and lovers of gain.','Plato',ARRAY['men','wisdom']::text[],'376390be45f352651f37deb1b74f971bed3b1a0e'),
('There are two things a person should never be angry at, what they can help, and what they cannot.','Plato',ARRAY['anger']::text[],'da0cf37913d181461c548780dcf3bffae2081d93'),
('All men are by nature equal, made all of the same earth by one Workman and however we deceive ourselves, as dear unto God is the poor peasant as the mighty prince.','Plato',ARRAY['god','men','nature']::text[],'0fc35d9110a49254904456d36163995daa84152f'),
('To love rightly is to love what is orderly and beautiful in an educated and disciplined way.','Plato',ARRAY['love']::text[],'346eb69641cca81bff74c763a5e49c8a4147471d'),
('Wise men speak because they have something to say Fools because they have to say something.','Plato',ARRAY['men']::text[],'e6de70520d5d9f8618a686e01921e1ec9a550268'),
('I would fain grow old learning many things.','Plato',ARRAY['learning']::text[],'5d7328fe62994bd9c2fe6adf7e48887de54cb08c'),
('He who steals a little steals with the same wish as he who steals much, but with less power.','Plato',ARRAY['power']::text[],'27e7b924c137428acee442114c95f17bdada3018'),
('Cunning... is but the low mimic of wisdom.','Plato',ARRAY['wisdom']::text[],'e458580a3807394b8ddabc1af5c684635ae68b4f'),
