('I exhort you also to take part in the great combat, which is the combat of life, and greater than every other earthly conflict.','Plato',ARRAY['great']::text[],'9b6199ed813ebaa551c7dafe96ab6c8b28a8e8d2'),
('Science is nothing but perception.','Plato',ARRAY['science']::text[],'27bfb332840b550b92301900d9f077bfc8483598'),
('The beginning is the most important part of the work.','Plato',ARRAY['art','work']::text[],'7e7dad18d30a128699d2e5b1584855f24c1bbfa0'),
('The learning and knowledge that we have, is, at the most, but little compared with that of which we are ignorant.','Plato',ARRAY['knowledge','learning']::text[],'dd5518f3a61372af2634f5e0162ce22895f0d52a'),
('They certainly give very strange names to diseases.','Plato',ARRAY['medical']::text[],'fc4ea279917b66ed7d73e9fa29b1e13b0f45a077'),
('Friendship is composed of a single soul inhabiting two bodies.','Plautus',ARRAY['friendship']::text[],'a4071ae0ba57003df4665133470d955eea060902'),
('Good courage in a bad affair is half of the evil overcome.','Plautus',ARRAY['courage']::text[],'d47f05b435da40562c26011baf31775eb49173f5'),
('Patience is the best remedy for every trouble.','Plautus',ARRAY['best','patience']::text[],'2bb19c942471cc29e87fb63d68ae38c8c041fc7e'),
('The day, water, sun, moon, night - I do not have to purchase these things with money.','Plautus',ARRAY['money']::text[],'8a43979dddc979499b8ffb51a8c0d3b162a1d4b0'),
('He whom the gods love dies young, while he is in health, has his senses and his judgments sound.','Plautus',ARRAY['health']::text[],'98c50764bae55922402a2a3952f152b11d9f18dd'),
('Nothing but heaven itself is better than a friend who is really a friend.','Plautus',ARRAY['friendship']::text[],'0b86907ccb5ddb1ee59a31169ccf021b42148033'),
('Let us celebrate the occasion with wine and sweet words.','Plautus',ARRAY['birthday']::text[],'9d586e54ef0c1edfd448b97b2069d9de6662f5a5'),
('Property is unstable, and youth perishes in a moment. Life itself is held in the grinning fangs of Death, Yet men delay to obtain release from the world. Alas, the conduct of mankind is surprising.','Plautus',ARRAY['death']::text[],'8101509f857ea71969861dba70b9db89cb327808'),
('Courage easily finds its own eloquence.','Plautus',ARRAY['courage']::text[],'ee9e48ceaa35b7500c1e4bed8927b31a96f42bb8'),
('Not by age but by capacity is wisdom acquired.','Plautus',ARRAY['age','wisdom']::text[],'3b1043fbaab3a30c6685459975872ac1aaba9898'),
('You must spend money to make money.','Plautus',ARRAY['money']::text[],'ac6f8b60441607110d0f9f52aa681fcde1888b10'),
('I would rather be adorned by beauty of character than jewels. Jewels are the gift of fortune, while character comes from within.','Plautus',ARRAY['beauty']::text[],'83161c54beed32cccdbd25d3cf82f0d186117199'),
('Courage in danger is half the battle.','Plautus',ARRAY['courage']::text[],'be2f3879927d5b1ee5b26aced82e08eadfaa963d'),
('Courage is what preserves our liberty, safety, life, and our homes and parents, our country and children. Courage comprises all things.','Plautus',ARRAY['courage']::text[],'7acad7d1a919e216e7fa4f79664df282e81095c0'),
('Wisdom is not attained by years, but by ability.','Plautus',ARRAY['wisdom']::text[],'75d9d704b4437e5d40b9511501fcce804df92263'),
('Hope is the pillar that holds up the world. Hope is the dream of a waking man.','Pliny the Elder',ARRAY['hope']::text[],'183748cbe9117fc6cac30c47cb81cab9d5382f0a'),
('Such is the audacity of man, that he hath learned to counterfeit Nature, yea, and is so bold as to challenge her in her work.','Pliny the Elder',ARRAY['nature']::text[],'9aedae02a7efc88353593583e4f3ae892394eb0b'),
('Home is where the heart is.','Pliny the Elder',ARRAY['home']::text[],'91f20d8b91219b48ea720bb5f7350c96bc45a864'),
('Truth comes out in wine.','Pliny the Elder',ARRAY['truth']::text[],'0c7be387370c676170290414715b863ffe088bf5'),
('Grief has limits, whereas apprehension has none. For we grieve only for what we know has happened, but we fear all that possibly may happen.','Pliny the Elder',ARRAY['fear']::text[],'58212814178dd502a1ee0184b87fd7dfe563929d'),
('What we achieve inwardly will change outer reality.','Plutarch',ARRAY['change','inspirational']::text[],'09fa186ad7afae716d245ff7c8134492c65e648a'),
('It is part of a good man to do great and noble deeds, though he risk everything.','Plutarch',ARRAY['great']::text[],'878aedb6a8b3caa423f3a3649315f403f6fc988c'),
('Courage stands halfway between cowardice and rashness, one of which is a lack, the other an excess of courage.','Plutarch',ARRAY['courage']::text[],'8d97a9071fe554e483e35c83730c761035ce46d1'),
('Silence at the proper season is wisdom, and better than any speech.','Plutarch',ARRAY['wisdom']::text[],'f68e189416ad4d06588fe3b44d6e117f815607ea'),
('I would rather excel in the knowledge of what is excellent, than in the extent of my power and possessions.','Plutarch',ARRAY['knowledge','power']::text[],'9ddf29068b7b88000d40c72cd9771ee4d86bf42d'),
('Courage consists not in hazarding without fear but being resolutely minded in a just cause.','Plutarch',ARRAY['courage','fear']::text[],'6e9f460a93db4e5b972695c7fc5851cecb9586f6'),
('Those who aim at great deeds must also suffer greatly.','Plutarch',ARRAY['great']::text[],'46d3689149377d0fabfdc73f3765f370a3fec7ec'),
('The mind is not a vessel to be filled but a fire to be kindled.','Plutarch',ARRAY['intelligence']::text[],'25cadacce9a1b5698c94ccde03822deb1f40a7cc'),
('Medicine to produce health must examine disease and music, to create harmony must investigate discord.','Plutarch',ARRAY['health','music']::text[],'33af2c687b34426fb5b883af77967e3aa29f1d20'),
('The omission of good is no less reprehensible than the commission of evil.','Plutarch',ARRAY['good']::text[],'e9fca8f9a10607d0c00538ae961f211e59565104'),
('The very spring and root of honesty and virtue lie in good education.','Plutarch',ARRAY['education']::text[],'15dc864f28040c3f78b3d54eef377a6addab7eb3'),
('To make no mistakes is not in the power of man but from their errors and mistakes the wise and good learn wisdom for the future.','Plutarch',ARRAY['future','good','learning','power','wisdom']::text[],'877d1068dfbc8f20f40716655b47a7babcd9d6dd'),
('The wildest colts make the best horses.','Plutarch',ARRAY['best']::text[],'0a56cfde07d6c4f8cf3358da875f060e54ab51ec'),
('It were better to have no opinion of God at all than such a one as is unworthy of him for the one is only belief - the other contempt.','Plutarch',ARRAY['god']::text[],'b5150e80ec9ecb3dd01d61ccd186db57c28a46fe'),
('I don''t need a friend who changes when I change and who nods when I nod my shadow does that much better.','Plutarch',ARRAY['change','friendship']::text[],'4817d4b4d1ddfbd3844c5fd77f381a378875c87b'),
('Painting is silent poetry, and poetry is painting that speaks.','Plutarch',ARRAY['poetry']::text[],'1f8c4c001f028b290905386b6f3aff38fbd25b5d'),
('Do not speak of your happiness to one less fortunate than yourself.','Plutarch',ARRAY['happiness']::text[],'f0de0c2670fbb65fdbc5d1d4f34f3151c044bb3e'),
('Yes, I was correctly quoted in saying I introduced sex into films in the 20''s, but it was sex in good taste and left a great deal to one''s imagination.','Pola Negri',ARRAY['imagination']::text[],'4dae113e4374471c4dff4c74a8b6e1a478550049'),
('The new pope knows that his task is to make the light of Christ shine before men and women of world - not his own light, but that of Christ.','Pope Benedict XVI',ARRAY['men','women']::text[],'0b04c25770a35d861264b3655f1f285c2dcfec3c'),
('Today, I, too, wish to reaffirm that I intend to continue on the path toward improved relations and friendship with the Jewish people, following the decisive lead given by John Paul II.','Pope Benedict XVI',ARRAY['friendship']::text[],'f9d6251727fd72f27ad659bbca6591e0991d62ea'),
('An Adult faith does not follow the waves of fashion and the latest novelties.','Pope Benedict XVI',ARRAY['faith','faith']::text[],'912c30eb40287f3e5a413b09b57fd9ca6e7f9bca'),
('I too hope in this short reign to be a man of peace.','Pope Benedict XVI',ARRAY['hope','peace']::text[],'9e86d76167d2215270ca806a64c78438455ab776'),
('The historical experience of socialist countries has sadly demonstrated that collectivism does not do away with alienation but rather increases it, adding to it a lack of basic necessities and economic inefficiency.','Pope John Paul II',ARRAY['experience']::text[],'6b2147e84a14548b346427ccfbf95c9a69ffc396'),
('I kiss the soil as if I placed a kiss on the hands of a mother, for the homeland is our earthly mother. I consider it my duty to be with my compatriots in this sublime and difficult moment.','Pope John Paul II',ARRAY['home']::text[],'13249d5bf12c7345f96ede934d1ebfe6f7cdee95'),
('Marriage is an act of will that signifies and involves a mutual gift, which unites the spouses and binds them to their eventual souls, with whom they make up a sole family - a domestic church.','Pope John Paul II',ARRAY['anniversary','family','marriage']::text[],'00a18f838e12966d36051b03f52670a65750db03'),
('The future starts today, not tomorrow.','Pope John Paul II',ARRAY['future']::text[],'64be220a89f7ac60fbe61f080a2df045d0c7eab6'),
('Radical changes in world politics leave America with a heightened responsibility to be, for the world, an example of a genuinely free, democratic, just and humane society.','Pope John Paul II',ARRAY['politics','society']::text[],'a5da2b578f2d30e071ea18b1af647975de9a2be5'),
('As the family goes, so goes the nation and so goes the whole world in which we live.','Pope John Paul II',ARRAY['family']::text[],'86fc7826237c9c10d15b7dfceb6b76d77fc5ede0'),
('The great danger for family life, in the midst of any society whose idols are pleasure, comfort and independence, lies in the fact that people close their hearts and become selfish.','Pope John Paul II',ARRAY['family','great','life','society']::text[],'47369bcad27282031b7f833df91c2106722dfd18'),
('I hope to have communion with the people, that is the most important thing.','Pope John Paul II',ARRAY['hope']::text[],'9124254196d8691a742f10af532eaceafe35bfb0'),
('To maintain a joyful family requires much from both the parents and the children. Each member of the family has to become, in a special way, the servant of the others.','Pope John Paul II',ARRAY['family']::text[],'325512a82975002809c4b19c882f2a0b953222cb'),
('Humanity should question itself, once more, about the absurd and always unfair phenomenon of war, on whose stage of death and pain only remain standing the negotiating table that could and should have prevented it.','Pope John Paul II',ARRAY['death','war']::text[],'301d60533a6c7ce18b1f44b936584acdecd966eb'),
('Freedom consists not in doing what we like, but in having the right to do what we ought.','Pope John Paul II',ARRAY['freedom']::text[],'70413cd0073876fcad641576d903ede05522a268'),
('Do not abandon yourselves to despair. We are the Easter people and hallelujah is our song.','Pope John Paul II',ARRAY['easter']::text[],'ac2c8e0f36e4b030d0c429137962f33c9a167cdf'),
('There are people and nations, Mother, that I would like to say to you by name. I entrust them to you in silence, I entrust them to you in the way that you know best.','Pope John Paul II',ARRAY['best']::text[],'692d0bc829e0a0dc164212ce5e952212fadf4e8e'),
('Love is never defeated, and I could add, the history of Ireland proves it.','Pope John Paul II',ARRAY['history','love','saintpatricksday']::text[],'4f09fdc09436add5ae9b1ebae8d7ec5eb126c3f3'),
('Science can purify religion from error and superstition. Religion can purify science from idolatry and false absolutes.','Pope John Paul II',ARRAY['religion','science']::text[],'0dd7b1ab0b30060a8b0839c5bcbd3fe4e1db4173'),
('I have a sweet tooth for song and music. This is my Polish sin.','Pope John Paul II',ARRAY['music']::text[],'0cdc2b6e818a9a5b55704f074308f79c1436891f'),
('Young people are threatened... by the evil use of advertising techniques that stimulate the natural inclination to avoid hard work by promising the immediate satisfaction of every desire.','Pope John Paul II',ARRAY['work']::text[],'1fab0c2a649de2f99234dd4e1f7dc3d116b7e88d'),
('Have no fear of moving into the unknown. Simply step out fearlessly knowing that I am with you, therefore no harm can befall you all is very, very well. Do this in complete faith and confidence.','Pope John Paul II',ARRAY['faith','fear']::text[],'c70ed7339e201af5dbc999d622dd92f1b8a2978e'),
('War is a defeat for humanity.','Pope John Paul II',ARRAY['war']::text[],'7312b1fd39a728ff589a4ff912d6e2cebc2db116'),
('Violence and arms can never resolve the problems of men.','Pope John Paul II',ARRAY['men']::text[],'eaeb1c8e571f2e1e1857a6d7c8135221d7f89faa'),
('What we talked about will have to remain a secret between him and me. I spoke to him as a brother whom I have pardoned and who has my complete trust.','Pope John Paul II',ARRAY['trust']::text[],'ea58d23ab0175b15b723f521fbd1fbd2e4277f15'),
('The unworthy successor of Peter who desires to benefit from the immeasurable wealth of Christ feels the great need of your assistance, your prayers, your sacrifice, and he most humbly asks this of you.','Pope John Paul II',ARRAY['great']::text[],'51f1990e14dce9703e0f5327d289fff0812a4524'),
('Stupidity is also a gift of God, but one mustn''t misuse it.','Pope John Paul II',ARRAY['god']::text[],'d786288c7ab88554091fe09cd23e85e41488fbe3'),
('It is easier for a father to have children than for children to have a real father.','Pope John XXIII',ARRAY['dad']::text[],'cf0bb0ba767e05b2f48c441e60af10872f17c2e0'),
('I have looked into your eyes with my eyes. I have put my heart near your heart.','Pope John XXIII',ARRAY['inspirational']::text[],'fecbb675f3cca4f11efee75e5e1617f6a34cc67a'),
('It is now for the Catholic Church to bend herself to her work with calmness and generosity. It is for you to observe her with renewed and friendly attention.','Pope John XXIII',ARRAY['work']::text[],'435845f79e7805ef9c0519df5f78d9e9f71bf98f'),
('The family is the first essential cell of human society.','Pope John XXIII',ARRAY['family','society']::text[],'552a94edfcbcc03338fdc1546b6649d7e701ffc1'),
('Men are like wine - some turn to vinegar, but the best improve with age.','Pope John XXIII',ARRAY['age','best','men']::text[],'efb721da7c07293521828cae3391a51958fac63c'),
('See everything, overlook a great deal, correct a little.','Pope John XXIII',ARRAY['great']::text[],'e4faf9c7dbd9847eab538e4dbf069b416f40536e'),
('The true and solid peace of nations consists not in equality of arms, but in mutual trust alone.','Pope John XXIII',ARRAY['alone','equality','peace','trust']::text[],'1a4391e2400141cab45bb1907f920af0ead3dc26'),
('I am able to follow my own death step by step. Now I move softly towards the end.','Pope John XXIII',ARRAY['death']::text[],'19006f82b723ec56d06e6dce6ac3125c64d24301'),
('Italians come to ruin most generally in three ways, women, gambling, and farming. My family chose the slowest one.','Pope John XXIII',ARRAY['family','women']::text[],'f9475b3722881a7ffff8677cbe1a93852609d1ba'),
('A peaceful man does more good than a learned one.','Pope John XXIII',ARRAY['good']::text[],'15213c528ee0aa5f0902bf732b6a6cceff58b1e0'),
('In youth the days are short and the years are long. In old age the years are short and day''s long.','Pope Paul VI',ARRAY['age']::text[],'128858b43a146d8a890d449cb9f302f4d4aea6a1'),
('Liturgy is like a strong tree whose beauty is derived from the continuous renewal of its leaves, but whose strength comes from the old trunk, with solid roots in the ground.','Pope Paul VI',ARRAY['beauty','strength']::text[],'e73a9283ebef45cc64159b1c2164de501809e22b'),
('Of all human activities, man''s listening to God is the supreme act of his reasoning and will.','Pope Paul VI',ARRAY['god','inspirational']::text[],'d109d8a2e7e2d6d35235e6f8c459f894f076592f'),
('Anger is as a stone cast into a wasp''s nest.','Pope Paul VI',ARRAY['anger']::text[],'18f49092307454668f181d2205210e28d008724c'),
('Nothing makes one feel so strong as a call for help.','Pope Paul VI',ARRAY['inspirational']::text[],'6cbc5177670c672abe0e374938c197213153da4b'),
('If you want peace work for justice.','Pope Paul VI',ARRAY['peace','work']::text[],'6c2093ed0fb81fc20ea301527b0494eaf8bf0619'),
('Technological society has succeeded in multiplying the opportunities for pleasure, but it has great difficulty in generating joy.','Pope Paul VI',ARRAY['society']::text[],'e4412f291557ebc07c728b7f3a1e121cb82ed43d'),
('We consider Christmas as the encounter, the great encounter, the historical encounter, the decisive encounter, between God and mankind. He who has faith knows this truly let him rejoice.','Pope Paul VI',ARRAY['faith','god','great','christmas']::text[],'d0b91a00ab76f6ff90c5bb481716e0de1cee6404'),
('No more war! Never again war! If you wish to be brothers, drop your weapons.','Pope Paul VI',ARRAY['war']::text[],'b8e4994e7e098c1692551af9291ac374e233596f'),
('The 4th Amendment and the personal rights it secures have a long history. At the very core stands the right of a man to retreat into his own home and there be free from unreasonable governmental intrusion.','Potter Stewart',ARRAY['history','home']::text[],'7ad67d936267e615ec1915d7b9b1b545e8358b64'),
('To force a lawyer on a defendant can only lead him to believe that the law contrives against him.','Potter Stewart',ARRAY['legal']::text[],'aec197e5438ef7661cb019dcb47d66922aa8cbf6'),
('Abortion is inherently different from other medical procedures because no other procedure involves the purposeful termination of a potential life.','Potter Stewart',ARRAY['medical']::text[],'3884e9bd0451c9da0123c0c5239ae9f0e332cf4b'),
('Freedom is an internal achievement rather than an external adjustment.','Powell Clayton',ARRAY['freedom']::text[],'014ed04867ce59472512ac2a05f7a1d2ba66fc63'),
('India-Seychelles relations have been characterized by close friendship, understanding and cooperation.','Pratibha Patil',ARRAY['friendship']::text[],'d916ec61e250f8265c82a6ee1fdf805e4f9d136b'),
('Women have talent and intelligence but, due to social constraints and prejudices, it is still a long distance away from the goal of gender equality.','Pratibha Patil',ARRAY['equality','intelligence']::text[],'0a76f603467eb2d5ac67fadd78311df321a54169'),
('This post of President is a Constitutional post. It is the duty of everyone, all citizens to see that they respect the post... the institution of President.','Pratibha Patil',ARRAY['respect']::text[],'6d48fba6b16ce928c2a88852f8873cf7fb1dda7d'),
('India is known for its sobriety and wisdom, balanced and sensible thinking. We need strong institutions and we need good governance in the country.','Pratibha Patil',ARRAY['wisdom']::text[],'f22d36b15bb44925ebd20b42963bfa553c526062'),
('I emphasize... that the Harrimans showed great courage and loyalty and confidence in us, because three or four of us were really running the business, the day to day business.','Prescott Bush',ARRAY['courage']::text[],'6afe6c8fdb816eb9946d562326ade692e542b996'),
('It is our conduct, our patriotism and belief in our American way of life, our courage that will win the final battle.','Prescott Bush',ARRAY['courage','patriotism']::text[],'78ad02a560d6071fc08444e5ad015d6302a19b8a'),
('Anyone who has obeyed nature by transmitting a piece of gossip experiences the explosive relief that accompanies the satisfying of a primary need.','Primo Levi',ARRAY['nature']::text[],'dafa33eb7bca849593a6a7d43228605701b16d85'),
('It is only the ignorant who despise education.','Publilius Syrus',ARRAY['education']::text[],'1ca6db79293682c4e5f38c81efc19f3be9cc81a6'),
('Art has a double face, of expression and illusion, just like science has a double face: the reality of error and the phantom of truth.','Publilius Syrus',ARRAY['art','science','truth']::text[],'8c0e14bcf3f95bfdd8ef767473e9e970012dbe39'),
('A good reputation is more valuable than money.','Publilius Syrus',ARRAY['good','money']::text[],'4dce210563b0deb7a478dbbbdb872ba4344b4677'),
('Valor grows by daring, fear by holding back.','Publilius Syrus',ARRAY['fear']::text[],'7e27864e6bb8f744bdab40baccbff4166fa8fa55'),
('How unhappy is he who cannot forgive himself.','Publilius Syrus',ARRAY['forgiveness']::text[],'fd814de1fb6bdb5c3a52506f1e49b8581eb9a5f4'),
('Audacity augments courage hesitation, fear.','Publilius Syrus',ARRAY['courage','fear']::text[],'857253a2e8590248741e5c2ab3744d2ed2a74b66'),
('Good health and good sense are two of life''s greatest blessings.','Publilius Syrus',ARRAY['good','health']::text[],'2db36150d4aa40ab42d9342f339d8a966470887f'),
('From the errors of others, a wise man corrects his own.','Publilius Syrus',ARRAY['wisdom']::text[],'9a5392b1ebb3424113922a7ced6382e4fbd3c25b'),
('An angry father is most cruel towards himself.','Publilius Syrus',ARRAY['dad']::text[],'417c258ced2f4d6723beac15282207c97542d793'),
('The bare recollection of anger kindles anger.','Publilius Syrus',ARRAY['anger']::text[],'83fe76b9bca7e8ae62189f953d34b1ddbda9b99e'),
('He whom many fear, has himself many to fear.','Publilius Syrus',ARRAY['fear']::text[],'bba5685eca40a087318a505af516a0fc9bb4d887'),
('There is geometry in the humming of the strings, there is music in the spacing of the spheres.','Pythagoras',ARRAY['music']::text[],'1cf0a1c0cc6281d1aa9b01650683e1c87d0b03b0'),
('Strength of mind rests in sobriety for this keeps your reason unclouded by passion.','Pythagoras',ARRAY['strength']::text[],'a09f636a168fc255d105e42118d8561daace1b79'),
('As soon as laws are necessary for men, they are no longer fit for freedom.','Pythagoras',ARRAY['freedom','men']::text[],'d4f335d9998c8ac8b91cc571e78e7f4b20248a1d'),
('It is better wither to be silent, or to say things of more value than silence. Sooner throw a pearl at hazard than an idle or useless word and do not say a little in many words, but a great deal in a few.','Pythagoras',ARRAY['great']::text[],'7a4bcc0de5c3330dcb6d633a4260616984177f67'),
('Friends are as companions on a journey, who ought to aid each other to persevere in the road to a happier life.','Pythagoras',ARRAY['life']::text[],'3dc1dcbb8101aeaf4e838c2b9683141597156c64'),
('As long as man continues to be the ruthless destroyer of lower living beings he will never know health or peace. For as long as men massacre animals, they will kill each other.','Pythagoras',ARRAY['health','men','peace']::text[],'67991b0df4b40df57eead0bc0a2a75a03422cdbc'),
('Great events make me quiet and calm it is only trifles that irritate my nerves.','Queen Victoria',ARRAY['great']::text[],'1724fb32a54cace0d7ddafef121f9923a1d35e22'),
('A marriage is no amusement but a solemn act, and generally a sad one.','Queen Victoria',ARRAY['marriage','sad']::text[],'2c0960fd29b86f9f934d09d79669bd56b244f5fc'),
('I think people really marry far too much it is such a lottery after all, and for a poor woman a very doubtful happiness.','Queen Victoria',ARRAY['happiness']::text[],'fb16c005f95eec546aecb0149201b9451367e3b2'),
('When I think of a merry, happy, free young girl - and look at the ailing, aching state a young wife generally is doomed to - which you can''t deny is the penalty of marriage.','Queen Victoria',ARRAY['marriage']::text[],'29cb74c602c77dc3fc7127bff922d864d88236ca'),
('It''s no good running a pig farm badly for 30 years while saying, ''Really, I was meant to be a ballet dancer.'' By then, pigs will be your style.','Quentin Crisp',ARRAY['good']::text[],'ed38cde3c41f3e64f114ab9dcbf8c8cb67b459b9'),
('The formula for achieving a successful relationship is simple: you should treat all disasters as if they were trivialities but never treat a triviality as if it were a disaster.','Quentin Crisp',ARRAY['relationship']::text[],'15bf13c8b6a0d9df92ce7b1ecf9d7635272e1346'),
('My mother protected me from the world and my father threatened me with it.','Quentin Crisp',ARRAY['parenting']::text[],'d12822f7566e916e88d75058967936240e6c0d01'),
('The British do not expect happiness. I had the impression, all the time that I lived there, that they do not want to be happy they want to be right.','Quentin Crisp',ARRAY['happiness']::text[],'d35d17bad9460d7df8ce6a22cb3f243db47cbd59'),
('Life was a funny thing that happened to me on the way to the grave.','Quentin Crisp',ARRAY['funny']::text[],'2f99e0ca3fe43214923cd50f03f20d562feccffd'),
('Though intelligence is powerless to modify character, it is a dab hand at finding euphemisms for its weaknesses.','Quentin Crisp',ARRAY['intelligence']::text[],'30aa6b781c0d079a64dfba00af81c313b1509e0d'),
('Men get laid, but women get screwed.','Quentin Crisp',ARRAY['women']::text[],'c09a938b0e2d008d6573bc9415a0c694999bfb28'),
('When I told the people of Northern Ireland that I was an atheist, a woman in the audience stood up and said, ''Yes, but is it the God of the Catholics or the God of the Protestants in whom you don''t believe?','Quentin Crisp',ARRAY['god']::text[],'4c343476e8938ec889ea02a94fe2fb88e340ec36'),
('Manners are love in a cool climate.','Quentin Crisp',ARRAY['cool']::text[],'2dd99e7de38885a715cfdca86fcb2b5fc1aff9c6'),
('It is not the simple statement of facts that ushers in freedom it is the constant repetition of them that has this liberating effect. Tolerance is the result not of enlightenment, but of boredom.','Quentin Crisp',ARRAY['freedom']::text[],'c04fb8f9e123aa3b39c67906a7df32121151c5f1'),
('For an introvert his environment is himself and can never be subject to startling or unforeseen change.','Quentin Crisp',ARRAY['change']::text[],'9c81b1d85803e2306bdd8413f63b7d765337b7b1'),
('If at first you don''t succeed, failure may be your style.','Quentin Crisp',ARRAY['failure']::text[],'e577247965fd215124f0a88bb723e8568e0e3d89'),
('Health consists of having the same diseases as one''s neighbors.','Quentin Crisp',ARRAY['health']::text[],'c34c65e2775ee67ec4de2d23c00ae41d0ffb7034'),
('It''s amazing how much trouble you can get in when you don''t have anything else to do.','Quincy Jones',ARRAY['amazing']::text[],'9a318cb5f0320c634751192fbddc5d25a4dc5b00'),
('Every country can be defined through their food, their music and their language. That''s the soul of a country.','Quincy Jones',ARRAY['food']::text[],'c6e00b54babdff2528c6d420ab850ff178031324'),
('Music in movies is all about dissonance and consonance, tension and release.','Quincy Jones',ARRAY['movies']::text[],'a552f96ee7cd7e87574885e02f9bed5d1b4213c9'),
('I started imagining this whole different world. It was a society of musicians, a family I hoped I could belong to one day.','Quincy Jones',ARRAY['society']::text[],'f4c4cc6cdf0a560c92a2d86b2930bb7c36850d05'),
('I was raised in Chicago and I guess that was one of the special breeding grounds for gangsters of all colors. That was the Detroit of the gangster world. The car industry was thugs.','Quincy Jones',ARRAY['car']::text[],'73ff3aef3362e0baced66420cec8bcd707eb8db6'),
('If you started in New York you were dealing with the biggest guys in the world. You''re dealing with Charlie Parker and all the big bands and everything. We got more experience working in Seattle.','Quincy Jones',ARRAY['experience']::text[],'eea5bf189b3b91112b5b4603c2b9c4479f852bbe'),
('I got a scholarship to Seattle University and I was writing arrangements for singers and everybody. But the music course was too dry and I really wanted to get away from home.','Quincy Jones',ARRAY['home']::text[],'b0b1dcef09509eaaefd51cf02a8915d36b2e241a'),
('If architecture is frozen music then music must be liquid architecture.','Quincy Jones',ARRAY['architecture','music']::text[],'a6417b237bb4a57b6ce9b00ae9d06886d1bbe1f8'),
('As regards parents, I should like to see them as highly educated as possible, and I do not restrict this remark to fathers alone.','Quintilian',ARRAY['alone']::text[],'ee8ed6b34696388fee8830b13f2c03c97cc9887b'),
('The gifts of nature are infinite in their variety, and mind differs from mind almost as much as body from body.','Quintilian',ARRAY['nature']::text[],'90296c5861a3db60af895f2293740f8aab122ea4'),
('Our minds are like our stomaches they are whetted by the change of their food, and variety supplies both with fresh appetite.','Quintilian',ARRAY['food']::text[],'651af2e49d302ff6672fb0a6101f416b1a11d561'),
('When we cannot hope to win, it is an advantage to yield.','Quintilian',ARRAY['hope']::text[],'d85cdf41a14ebc301558b042e564db02b1a36637'),
('Forbidden pleasures alone are loved immoderately when lawful, they do not excite desire.','Quintilian',ARRAY['alone']::text[],'01be7349b58d161a3e53e9176a35ec289f8fea20'),
('The perfection of art is to conceal art.','Quintilian',ARRAY['art']::text[],'4381b77f86ec83de732bf18c478f2834d006840d'),
('To my mind the boy who gives least promise is one in whom the critical faculty develops in advance of the imagination.','Quintilian',ARRAY['imagination']::text[],'69692c312a63a1185b7a2268f7d8ca2583b6550b'),
('In almost everything, experience is more valuable than precept.','Quintilian',ARRAY['experience']::text[],'30b0895fc5c91a0a7b312942a87e68249511ca1a'),
('Men, even when alone, lighten their labors by song, however rude it may be.','Quintilian',ARRAY['alone','men']::text[],'21ca14fed4f1d0fcf0bf8ef2d8a0c2de7903d2b6'),
('Vain hopes are like certain dreams of those who wake.','Quintilian',ARRAY['dreams']::text[],'0ca6495e011ea2533c1047e947a61f449cfcb421'),
('Fear of the future is worse than one''s present fortune.','Quintilian',ARRAY['fear','future']::text[],'708e3123d9d434c033be5ec5ce50642a867a55c3'),
('It is worth while too to warn the teacher that undue severity in correcting faults is liable at times to discourage a boy''s mind from effort.','Quintilian',ARRAY['teacher']::text[],'91d4c8582afc1c47b6f3694a298cf9f90ed3d6fc'),
('We are all murderers and prostitutes - no matter to what culture, society, class, nation one belongs, no matter how normal, moral, or mature, one takes oneself to be.','R. D. Laing',ARRAY['society']::text[],'c674ef9a0b7cf898e396495a528c9e12e8141dc1'),
('Children do not give up their innate imagination, curiosity, dreaminess easily. You have to love them to get them to do that.','R. D. Laing',ARRAY['imagination']::text[],'fece78971bb4512c0046358515bccc5a82228ea9'),
('Madness need not be all breakdown. It may also be break-through. It is potential liberation and renewal as well as enslavement and existential death.','R. D. Laing',ARRAY['death']::text[],'5d6e5c23715dc181b89ca7fffd11ad345057ae53'),
('We live in a moment of history where change is so speeded up that we begin to see the present only when it is already disappearing.','R. D. Laing',ARRAY['change','history']::text[],'c0ccb62dc47cb9e266c88c5a0173dbe2aee37b37'),
('There is a great deal of pain in life and perhaps the only pain that can be avoided is the pain that comes from trying to avoid pain.','R. D. Laing',ARRAY['great']::text[],'0ed17acf636d36247c73954167bec18d4a18a77e'),
('The experience and behavior that gets labeled schizophrenic is a special strategy that a person invents in order to live in an unlivable situation.','R. D. Laing',ARRAY['experience']::text[],'93813fcebba7013b2745da4f45673a444b3940a3'),
('The highest education is that which does not merely give us information but makes our life in harmony with all existence.','Rabindranath Tagore',ARRAY['education','life']::text[],'144f9ea0806896660873e11a07a7402ff4b11bd1'),
('Death is not extinguishing the light it is only putting out the lamp because the dawn has come.','Rabindranath Tagore',ARRAY['death']::text[],'ee6f36046a7431e66c7a1a54ed9f7956353654bd'),
('The butterfly counts not months but moments, and has time enough.','Rabindranath Tagore',ARRAY['nature','time']::text[],'dc1ec2ca2fce923b217480e14e65c9c6f06c30d8'),
('We gain freedom when we have paid the full price.','Rabindranath Tagore',ARRAY['freedom']::text[],'4ad7ea3ffbefcef0aaf584b69048e5468d2285b4'),
('Your idol is shattered in the dust to prove that God''s dust is greater than your idol.','Rabindranath Tagore',ARRAY['god']::text[],'f7997c361dd65b6bf85a1dc33f597c673d3533bd'),
('Do not say, ''It is morning,'' and dismiss it with a name of yesterday. See it for the first time as a newborn child that has no name.','Rabindranath Tagore',ARRAY['morning','time']::text[],'9fe9dd9c3ee69ffca38e8ddf9cdfa070aea82bbf'),
('Love does not claim possession, but gives freedom.','Rabindranath Tagore',ARRAY['freedom','love']::text[],'e4d33d6cea718e3cba7fbaf0e3545b6a78f60de0'),
('Let your life lightly dance on the edges of Time like dew on the tip of a leaf.','Rabindranath Tagore',ARRAY['time']::text[],'2238dd19a24666f4b5cb598925fe9fd4b27cb35a'),
('Facts are many, but the truth is one.','Rabindranath Tagore',ARRAY['truth']::text[],'8f5b0be5f9ee4da70d67b5cd06f53116e187b48f'),
('We come nearest to the great when we are great in humility.','Rabindranath Tagore',ARRAY['great']::text[],'0592c1bfc5f51623e1864bc9810a174438c090d0'),
('Beauty is truth''s smile when she beholds her own face in a perfect mirror.','Rabindranath Tagore',ARRAY['beauty','smile','truth']::text[],'06dc195662d82a82181f8302f4e2d184a32692d4'),
('Love is not a mere impulse, it must contain truth, which is law.','Rabindranath Tagore',ARRAY['truth']::text[],'a11d312f567aef3171d74f5749902bbf71e0016d'),
('To be outspoken is easy when you do not wait to speak the complete truth.','Rabindranath Tagore',ARRAY['truth']::text[],'6b7bd00cd987c1b78157d1bcbf76809d65e0b50d'),
('From the solemn gloom of the temple children run out to sit in the dust, God watches them play and forgets the priest.','Rabindranath Tagore',ARRAY['god']::text[],'78c11e5f6a931afa8c6a0e18a03cdbf8efb1e970'),
('By plucking her petals, you do not gather the beauty of the flower.','Rabindranath Tagore',ARRAY['beauty']::text[],'aefc0b7d7ee7105050c767f1006a47881e28a9e7'),
('Bigotry tries to keep truth safe in its hand with a grip that kills it.','Rabindranath Tagore',ARRAY['truth']::text[],'bf99ad126a0a1aef559f7013d51bea42753ae589'),
('Emancipation from the bondage of the soil is no freedom for the tree.','Rabindranath Tagore',ARRAY['freedom']::text[],'8f2ca2b407c15d61ade02460e8dbfce2ccf16bdd'),
('Love is the only reality and it is not a mere sentiment. It is the ultimate truth that lies at the heart of creation.','Rabindranath Tagore',ARRAY['love','truth']::text[],'3874926e74085a0bae6665528b4927ba9b08b7cc'),
('Depth of friendship does not depend on length of acquaintance.','Rabindranath Tagore',ARRAY['friendship']::text[],'f5791c2a9fd339a2ce03249bff0eb3d869310d21'),
('He who is too busy doing good finds no time to be good.','Rabindranath Tagore',ARRAY['good','time']::text[],'de6b9433a2a3859d78a0d4492c36ce1dc138872a'),
('Clouds come floating into my life, no longer to carry rain or usher storm, but to add color to my sunset sky.','Rabindranath Tagore',ARRAY['inspirational','life']::text[],'616de019e252faa2cc895ebb138ae55bd87753a0'),
('I slept and dreamt that life was joy. I awoke and saw that life was service. I acted and behold, service was joy.','Rabindranath Tagore',ARRAY['life']::text[],'94255cd8dd83e95636bd7f78e4f9382e6d1ddd29'),
('Those who own much have much to fear.','Rabindranath Tagore',ARRAY['fear']::text[],'18f7960304975ea8cd59940dfbd3e0c4885e9109'),
('What is Art? It is the response of man''s creative soul to the call of the Real.','Rabindranath Tagore',ARRAY['art']::text[],'7259805c1512b8781d353f8c015d367028e71c21'),
('Don''t limit a child to your own learning, for he was born in another time.','Rabindranath Tagore',ARRAY['education','learning','time']::text[],'dc0a75e34fce1fdfec3702bbdfc46986ae2a62ac'),
('Every child comes with the message that God is not yet discouraged of man.','Rabindranath Tagore',ARRAY['god']::text[],'7222093c6710b762c72810b954791fa23cff6afb'),
('Age considers youth ventures.','Rabindranath Tagore',ARRAY['age']::text[],'90f49ae47a0de18256301b3b4560e08abe8033e9'),
('Gray hairs are signs of wisdom if you hold your tongue, speak and they are but hairs, as in the young.','Rabindranath Tagore',ARRAY['wisdom']::text[],'2099b3c5300e43ff0e4368c8749bb4e46dfe25c6'),
('If you shut the door to all errors, truth will be shut out.','Rabindranath Tagore',ARRAY['truth']::text[],'ec640f548cc9d4062ecc380870f2000bda05e388'),
('Music fills the infinite between two souls.','Rabindranath Tagore',ARRAY['music']::text[],'4f8116dd8f0d85b61e80acd6c99bfea58787db1d'),
('In Art, man reveals himself and not his objects.','Rabindranath Tagore',ARRAY['art']::text[],'f69f11eb5deff2ac32e5484c60d17a68950cbb97'),
('Faith is the bird that feels the light when the dawn is still dark.','Rabindranath Tagore',ARRAY['faith']::text[],'f14de59f7da5c648133553cc4c2ec8d997c9567d'),
('Trees are the earth''s endless effort to speak to the listening heaven.','Rabindranath Tagore',ARRAY['nature']::text[],'691f53fab65d0dfafde7a0c59f66778474fe8181'),
('Love is an endless mystery, for it has nothing else to explain it.','Rabindranath Tagore',ARRAY['love']::text[],'cd903624475c647dcf2c677e51f89baf5467fcda'),
('The water in a vessel is sparkling the water in the sea is dark. The small truth has words which are clear the great truth has great silence.','Rabindranath Tagore',ARRAY['great','truth']::text[],'c5694c0c4e2646d5e026cfd1782106a113f1b3e3'),
('Too much good fortune can make you smug and unaware. Happiness should be like an oasis, the greener for the desert that surrounds it.','Rachel Field',ARRAY['happiness']::text[],'0d8c9fd4e63c2b7596805f37ece207b565d009c3'),
('The main thing is that it''s nice to see these young people - 9 to 14 years old - take the opportunity to get more involved in their health and fitness. We need more kids to be more active.','Rafer Johnson',ARRAY['fitness','health']::text[],'ad482ea52391c98919ef705d76a211bf5345772b'),
('The future enters into us, in order to transform itself in us, long before it happens.','Rainer Maria Rilke',ARRAY['future']::text[],'c49259e26dfc6608aba666a5ff1c06c197150da5'),
('Love consists in this, that two solitudes protect and touch and greet each other.','Rainer Maria Rilke',ARRAY['love']::text[],'05be0858df1369e40ddf6479f8dd3372fd57996c'),
('I want to be with those who know secret things or else alone.','Rainer Maria Rilke',ARRAY['alone']::text[],'939069a33537b21beb8b8b5515220f6a79511db3'),
('No great art has ever been made without the artist having known danger.','Rainer Maria Rilke',ARRAY['art','great']::text[],'19c4a624c115119892e21d3785bee5ff042b63f0'),
('This is the miracle that happens every time to those who really love: the more they give, the more they possess.','Rainer Maria Rilke',ARRAY['love','time']::text[],'b4ac0375fa31f0e51f839a647b00cb591d74c21c'),
('Believe that with your feelings and your work you are taking part in the greatest the more strongly you cultivate this belief, the more will reality and the world go forth from it.','Rainer Maria Rilke',ARRAY['work']::text[],'2d9224b39eead24672aca17601e88e808727bf32'),
('A person isn''t who they are during the last conversation you had with them - they''re who they''ve been throughout your whole relationship.','Rainer Maria Rilke',ARRAY['relationship']::text[],'9498a037cf986e29a021934e1ee26c4e5ba38658'),
('The deepest experience of the creator is feminine, for it is experience of receiving and bearing.','Rainer Maria Rilke',ARRAY['experience']::text[],'66fa4b57c4105e9e66a16df551330473aa8e8ce7'),
('For one human being to love another that is perhaps the most difficult of all our tasks, the ultimate, the last test and proof, the work for which all other work is but preparation.','Rainer Maria Rilke',ARRAY['love','work']::text[],'04551f2555dc9e7a032bab66775b1d8798e9e5d3'),
('One had to take some action against fear when once it laid hold of one.','Rainer Maria Rilke',ARRAY['fear']::text[],'4a7c44af98af472af7ed97cc104e58d6bde9ac79'),
('Everything is blooming most recklessly if it were voices instead of colors, there would be an unbelievable shrieking into the heart of the night.','Rainer Maria Rilke',ARRAY['nature']::text[],'9faa0bee31ec8236c0ab6f1e6c92ba221e4b30e3'),
('More belongs to marriage than four legs in a bed.','Rainer Maria Rilke',ARRAY['marriage']::text[],'e9328739089525435dbaece87b4a682a4b64c147'),
('Surely all art is the result of one''s having been in danger, of having gone through an experience all the way to the end, where no one can go any further.','Rainer Maria Rilke',ARRAY['art','experience']::text[],'7e486e8af3b529d04b2bad056553e55a51054132'),
('Christians should be ready for a change because Jesus was the greatest changer in history.','Ralph Abernathy',ARRAY['change','history']::text[],'8e38097c57e3fd4a6cfbda6e10cd8da5384f8aa7'),
('I don''t know what the future may hold, but I know who holds the future.','Ralph Abernathy',ARRAY['future']::text[],'5932bbabeb611bc69a1e10390d04984ae3804f2c'),
('One of the best animated films I''ve seen come out of Disney was the Tarzan movie. I wasn''t crazy about the story or the design on Tarzan''s face, but the traditional animation was spectacular.','Ralph Bakshi',ARRAY['design']::text[],'9a9547c521df7a1faffbac338c55c881f6e7215e'),
('To this day I don''t ever remember seeing a pet inside Moscow, I never saw anyone carrying a dog, or leading a dog. Err I finally saw a, a pet some years later in Kiev, so I thought that life must have been, different.','Ralph Boston',ARRAY['pet']::text[],'57e2e11af1dec42b14aa250ee34fe721370f905a'),
('To make our way, we must have firm resolve, persistence, tenacity. We must gear ourselves to work hard all the way. We can never let up.','Ralph Bunche',ARRAY['work']::text[],'d8573e5d4dff568b73a4d311fb98ae06a334fb01'),
('The working class owes all honor and respect to the first men who planted the standard of labor solidarity on the hostile frontier of unorganized industry.','Ralph Chaplin',ARRAY['respect']::text[],'16143e087f461911327f43128563eb9408edb42f'),
('Knowledge is not a passion from without the mind, but an active exertion of the inward strength, vigor and power of the mind, displaying itself from within.','Ralph Cudworth',ARRAY['knowledge','power','strength']::text[],'16f6c32acc5ede1bd4877c11f7d3ab8061c65d33'),
('Now all the knowledge and wisdom that is in creatures, whether angels or men, is nothing else but a participation of that one eternal, immutable and increased wisdom of God.','Ralph Cudworth',ARRAY['knowledge','wisdom']::text[],'b885c31ef78324adc450e4c991d935004d761c8e'),
('Education is all a matter of building bridges.','Ralph Ellison',ARRAY['education']::text[],'13e0c063743f13b531af376d61a3085103c9c328'),
('Some people are your relatives but others are your ancestors, and you choose the ones you want to have as ancestors. You create yourself out of those values.','Ralph Ellison',ARRAY['relationship']::text[],'88fe4fee8ab81f19611013fc1a11c8c2d816878b'),
('The understanding of art depends finally upon one''s willingness to extend one''s humanity and one''s knowledge of human life.','Ralph Ellison',ARRAY['knowledge']::text[],'904d388edbebae5065e6f7b3e2f7dbbabf2d80ab'),
('It''s the kind of clothes that mothers and daughters can wear, in terms of concept... It''s not about age. It''s about taste, and it''s about lifestyle. I believe women of all ages can wear anything.','Ralph Lauren',ARRAY['age','women']::text[],'b23be5c142e2d2fdeadb03b948e93acf3d16795f'),
('People ask how can a Jewish kid from the Bronx do preppy clothes? Does it have to do with class and money? It has to do with dreams.','Ralph Lauren',ARRAY['dreams','money']::text[],'f4e014eade6680ef3f7aee9c339de06388747dfc'),
('I don''t design clothes, I design dreams.','Ralph Lauren',ARRAY['design','dreams']::text[],'bda7ed15960281e70ec22faf112a29b34f9bcfa6'),
('The keys to patience are acceptance and faith. Accept things as they are, and look realistically at the world around you. Have faith in yourself and in the direction you have chosen.','Ralph Marston',ARRAY['faith','patience']::text[],'7f0cded173479a948647dea9c27f091ab93c9c0a'),
('Don''t lower your expectations to meet your performance. Raise your level of performance to meet your expectations. Expect the best of yourself, and then do what is necessary to make it a reality.','Ralph Marston',ARRAY['best']::text[],'753ed513a5235b8daef405ef61077181e4fa3261'),
('Success in any endeavor depends on the degree to which it is an expression of your true self.','Ralph Marston',ARRAY['success']::text[],'b66fd7f29c98993be19ff417aebfa7f3971f44de'),
('You''ve done it before and you can do it now. See the positive possibilities. Redirect the substantial energy of your frustration and turn it into positive, effective, unstoppable determination.','Ralph Marston',ARRAY['positive']::text[],'d13461ebafde1bade4b1ba3e336479cbd7028b21'),
('Excellence is not a skill. It is an attitude.','Ralph Marston',ARRAY['attitude','experience']::text[],'d0c2afd7c4904d62aa9e7cf4310a6201a3935278'),
('Rest when you''re weary. Refresh and renew yourself, your body, your mind, your spirit. Then get back to work.','Ralph Marston',ARRAY['health','work']::text[],'bc75c9f39455a3299d28991a4ae5e5429b18acaf'),
('What you do today can improve all your tomorrows.','Ralph Marston',ARRAY['motivational']::text[],'6cf24cdff4b7754353788e7b9db0f2264cd0384a'),
('Beset by a difficult problem? Now is your chance to shine. Pick yourself up, get to work and get triumphantly through it.','Ralph Marston',ARRAY['work']::text[],'84cc05310762d8f724590c16d18f351e95577687'),
('Like sex in Victorian England, the reality of Big Business today is our big dirty secret.','Ralph Nader',ARRAY['business']::text[],'571444817ad16b794f1a05e06efee38804daca4a'),
('Addiction should never be treated as a crime. It has to be treated as a health problem. We do not send alcoholics to jail in this country. Over 500,000 people are in our jails who are nonviolent drug users.','Ralph Nader',ARRAY['health']::text[],'2f18d8345c182c48cbac8438fe131a5102e26855'),
('Every time I see something terrible, it''s like I see it at age 19. I keep a freshness that way.','Ralph Nader',ARRAY['age']::text[],'4eec899fdaaf433e4d49301742430d57520c11f0'),
('John D. Rockefeller wanted to dominate oil, but Microsoft wants it all, you name it: cable, media, banking, car dealerships.','Ralph Nader',ARRAY['car']::text[],'d8d2e948949250a8f988b7dce94fc050119e63b7'),
('People are stunned to hear that one company has data files on 185 million Americans.','Ralph Nader',ARRAY['technology']::text[],'f089789dfb9e03bd4733f82b749a617b47f74f8f'),
('The nation is faced with one of the most corporate-orientated anti-consumer Congresses in our history.','Ralph Nader',ARRAY['history']::text[],'5672b9996bf78f3ca1de371e6394a5549d36b659'),
('A society that has more justice is a society that needs less charity.','Ralph Nader',ARRAY['society']::text[],'c41b3046603c0bf4bf19b72ea2dff3388fe6c3a8'),
('Power has to be insecure to be responsive.','Ralph Nader',ARRAY['power']::text[],'20be53f62f4ad0a660199be704606cf2f45bccb2'),
('A leader has the vision and conviction that a dream can be achieved. He inspires the power and energy to get it done.','Ralph Nader',ARRAY['power']::text[],'01d41890a084ab58463de5ffc7a896067129db2e'),
('I don''t think meals have any business being deductible. I''m for separation of calories and corporations.','Ralph Nader',ARRAY['business']::text[],'aba3704aa8b8342189e190fa17fc8413d6bfab7e'),
('The function of leadership is to produce more leaders, not more followers.','Ralph Nader',ARRAY['leadership']::text[],'7778cad6ba56b4a2329cf1007ade28d61276c339'),
('I start with the premise that the function of leadership is to produce more leaders, not more followers.','Ralph Nader',ARRAY['leadership']::text[],'85c0a2a71456974eb4a1902e0f37b2bce5fb0b7c'),
('I once said to my father, when I was a boy, ''Dad we need a third political party.'' He said to me, ''I''ll settle for a second.''','Ralph Nader',ARRAY['dad']::text[],'34f9a961e73e9102ff99677853ec19fb9a74c9f5'),
('Your best teacher is your last mistake.','Ralph Nader',ARRAY['best','teacher']::text[],'07463319d4541cd98a848438b8b93eecf09b59e0'),
('President Reagan was elected on the promise of getting government off the backs of the people and now he demands that government wrap itself around the waists of the people.','Ralph Nader',ARRAY['government']::text[],'2dc7d6dd6901a8a7fa2b7933ba6223b256bd17a8'),
('Turn on to politics, or politics will turn on you.','Ralph Nader',ARRAY['politics']::text[],'ccfe35fb9745816775d77241f756b06342941ce1'),
('I''m thankful that I have lived long enough to become a legend, and I hope I deserve it.','Ralph Stanley',ARRAY['thankful']::text[],'b012ff6e112e32b9df39e36e1aaac7827f9478fe'),
('I''ve done it all. I''m thankful and proud of what I''ve accomplished in my life. I hope to keep doing it.','Ralph Stanley',ARRAY['thankful']::text[],'8baac5553e241daaa81a088b77763e7f1b618b85'),
('It makes me so desperately sad to witness just how unforgivably wretched our world has become.','Ralph Steadman',ARRAY['sad']::text[],'39c937baa6121971a58031d893746f5dfc82923a'),
('You see that''s what I think is such a terrible, terrible betrayal, the trust that people have in government.','Ralph Steadman',ARRAY['trust']::text[],'bcdb1b4f32b78553009c6911b1ac2e4eecb846f2'),
('All I have seen teaches me to trust the creator for all I have not seen.','Ralph Waldo Emerson',ARRAY['trust']::text[],'66ec941a22e337bf06a277c0a3a5933ee5383f2a'),
('Nothing astonishes men so much as common sense and plain dealing.','Ralph Waldo Emerson',ARRAY['men']::text[],'92e4fdbe82389fef8e07466a1f46e93a15957ab9'),
('Truth is the property of no individual but is the treasure of all men.','Ralph Waldo Emerson',ARRAY['men','truth']::text[],'df72795c7f124e5c040b2107f5c45f9527f64bfa'),
('God enters by a private door into every individual.','Ralph Waldo Emerson',ARRAY['faith','god']::text[],'61d8bcf6f1e621b8eef1b661e1c456954ba152ef'),
('Enthusiasm is the mother of effort, and without it nothing great was ever achieved.','Ralph Waldo Emerson',ARRAY['great']::text[],'7e0e4755db49815aed342b4d09ff4cff68840244'),
('The faith that stands on authority is not faith.','Ralph Waldo Emerson',ARRAY['faith']::text[],'d16661fbf5d1acfd22d0947da7781cc60678d959'),
('Genius always finds itself a century too early.','Ralph Waldo Emerson',ARRAY['intelligence']::text[],'708d46c45ad6a67d93535e165a8d90618cfc6ed8'),
('Nothing external to you has any power over you.','Ralph Waldo Emerson',ARRAY['power']::text[],'9b84b6e24ecf472394e767d514191bdfe2aaa6a7'),
('Adopt the pace of nature: her secret is patience.','Ralph Waldo Emerson',ARRAY['nature','patience','wisdom']::text[],'b00389e7ec6ad71d4769c21273b87b2c0f33cc05'),
('Society is always taken by surprise at any new example of common sense.','Ralph Waldo Emerson',ARRAY['society']::text[],'bc1089f440606163d2eb9e856d9ac4a856a053f1'),
('Manners require time, and nothing is more vulgar than haste.','Ralph Waldo Emerson',ARRAY['time']::text[],'0a795ff46e96a0cb612b102ed1b0c4e1289323be'),
('Science does not know its debt to imagination.','Ralph Waldo Emerson',ARRAY['imagination','science']::text[],'e9c38e3f684e4a27e8604e52f383607e98cf65f3'),
('We find delight in the beauty and happiness of children that makes the heart too big for the body.','Ralph Waldo Emerson',ARRAY['beauty','happiness']::text[],'e1c413ab379c5218bbd4658b7d47a5b4305af8eb'),
('Friendship, like the immortality of the soul, is too good to be believed.','Ralph Waldo Emerson',ARRAY['friendship','good']::text[],'2af703d0a4bc7d3f7107554dcfb1a0f8671fed0d'),
('Every mind must make its choice between truth and repose. It cannot have both.','Ralph Waldo Emerson',ARRAY['truth']::text[],'8b476e490d7d9d14b31cadb262d255b30e05c862'),
('A man is usually more careful of his money than he is of his principles.','Ralph Waldo Emerson',ARRAY['money']::text[],'02a300523bf9444a5b63b6e7c2112e73c4b5e170'),
('A man is relieved and gay when he has put his heart into his work and done his best but what he has said or done otherwise shall give him no peace.','Ralph Waldo Emerson',ARRAY['best','peace','work']::text[],'218fc4a3d56f121bb7d01456966abe7a231133df'),
('The search after the great men is the dream of youth, and the most serious occupation of manhood.','Ralph Waldo Emerson',ARRAY['great','men']::text[],'2780bcaf3ab75daad03212b72fb8578b13a4ec70'),
('No change of circumstances can repair a defect of character.','Ralph Waldo Emerson',ARRAY['change']::text[],'1d25800af4827aa25d3dab28c61f138df7c47334'),
('A man is a god in ruins. When men are innocent, life shall be longer, and shall pass into the immortal, as gently as we awake from dreams.','Ralph Waldo Emerson',ARRAY['dreams','god','life','men']::text[],'d8218d3ea24b2b4da2c8f345533d4268bfbaefc7'),
('The age of a woman doesn''t mean a thing. The best tunes are played on the oldest fiddles.','Ralph Waldo Emerson',ARRAY['age','best','women']::text[],'02fd3eb4dde2b75820be686bf935e419cf4a9073'),
('The reason why men do not obey us, is because they see the mud at the bottom of our eye.','Ralph Waldo Emerson',ARRAY['men']::text[],'598e8b76000cf0ad78e5739ecc26950edadb7127'),
('Do not go where the path may lead, go instead where there is no path and leave a trail.','Ralph Waldo Emerson',ARRAY['wisdom']::text[],'c586bcae81e6628d4e6646a61db7ab8d0e64852b'),
('We see God face to face every hour, and know the savor of Nature.','Ralph Waldo Emerson',ARRAY['god','nature']::text[],'b196f07f0d84401fb0be38690bdb6d5512c98412'),
