('The evil that men do lives after them the good is oft interred with their bones.','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['good','men']::text[],'6708893fe1c65d3782ddf5a22c8252f433cd6871'),
('It is a wise father that knows his own child.','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['fathersday']::text[],'bf6bbf65ca90829675a0ece0402393484c813609'),
('Cowards die many times before their deaths the valiant never taste of death but once.','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['death']::text[],'5e0d8d664c7d08cb796a0d8190095187e80e7e6e'),
('One touch of nature makes the whole world kin.','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['nature']::text[],'7dbfa30a171dc571f953e9687bfcbdaa35438969'),
('Life every man holds dear but the dear man holds honor far more precious dear than life.','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['life']::text[],'37880b6444167a3b85fd8342157761ccaac21613'),
('For I can raise no money by vile means.','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['money']::text[],'03bb5542e0faee8510f1026d44a1a9f3acec98c5'),
('If music be the food of love, play on.','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['food','love','music']::text[],'0edf6ff3378c65b3bee70d32153b88dbd8195f99'),
('No, I will be the pattern of all patience I will say nothing.','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['patience']::text[],'728d89aaec84775cd9f798e1138a735d2fdfcba0'),
('Our doubts are traitors and make us lose the good we oft might win by fearing to attempt.','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['good']::text[],'765d48cb2812017f3f7d50362c330d645bfc2fa8'),
('Many a good hanging prevents a bad marriage.','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['good','marriage']::text[],'919f44adbdd37430d3bc3f5a59f0c1c2364f4a29'),
('Life is as tedious as twice-told tale, vexing the dull ear of a drowsy man.','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['life']::text[],'3eae81c59a89fd28b796ed8b260eb5cf85f6fe33'),
('The man that hath no music in himself, Nor is not moved with concord of sweet sounds, is fit for treasons, stratagems and spoils.','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['music']::text[],'8ddf5f834a5f359b27687db15e8411233df92032'),
('Come, gentlemen, I hope we shall drink down all unkindness.','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['hope','newyears']::text[],'51b7463b8d979fb1f35e8b26658641904c1ed98f'),
('I had rather have a fool to make me merry than experience to make me sad and to travel for it too!','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['experience','sad','travel']::text[],'c2c0186091f13732effcecbd47b0b706349a4ad0'),
('Love is a smoke made with the fume of sighs.','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['love']::text[],'d4d480d9bff3de6891821e4ab70d0b60f2af56ce'),
('There is nothing either good or bad but thinking makes it so.','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['good']::text[],'c995993c96308261e3b45e412245f029becdc052'),
('Ignorance is the curse of God knowledge is the wing wherewith we fly to heaven.','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['god','intelligence','knowledge']::text[],'db34eb8d441009ef00dc17eaf77680a5a11e9fe4'),
('Now, God be praised, that to believing souls gives light in darkness, comfort in despair.','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['faith','god']::text[],'2ae627095ceaf94539b3e68ec7940d2aa474ee78'),
('Men''s vows are women''s traitors!','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['men','women']::text[],'4bb40ec531b19097a52e4defed000356c5209e3b'),
('Men shut their doors against a setting sun.','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['men']::text[],'9c627ef743fb8446ba6a9ac669e0aefc16034ad9'),
('They do not love that do not show their love.','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['love']::text[],'292dd23cf1a819bb158caa8eee68086fe7de6d84'),
('The stroke of death is as a lover''s pinch, which hurts and is desired.','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['death']::text[],'8ab9f47b537ef478d917187cb913d227e1d3d170'),
('There''s no art to find the mind''s construction in the face.','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['art']::text[],'c02068106016811ebf56ffbe5943e5956664b29d'),
('The course of true love never did run smooth.','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['love']::text[],'8cd8f5fcb1d73f919965e1244e453261dfbb457f'),
('I hold the world but as the world, Gratiano A stage where every man must play a part, And mine is a sad one.','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['sad']::text[],'f59e6a6d9d0fe690d12dd2f32b744c1a49ef6c46'),
('If to do were as easy as to know what were good to do, chapels had been churches, and poor men''s cottage princes'' palaces.','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['good','men']::text[],'bf460c0debcbd68183a096828c2d210c7e22db45'),
('Good night, good night! Parting is such sweet sorrow, that I shall say good night till it be morrow.','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['good','romantic']::text[],'93df3079d1c6b37a0a7e90425594a5a36bf56aba'),
('How far that little candle throws its beams! So shines a good deed in a naughty world.','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['good']::text[],'fa38efe3f5d7d1cff66dd6ae8a8f919b951237ca'),
('O God, O God, how weary, stale, flat, and unprofitable seem to me all the uses of this world!','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['god']::text[],'9fb66d01334583198b121f3208d333c9798105e0'),
('We are time''s subjects, and time bids be gone.','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['time']::text[],'38f0e4c195af443a89c23f0ff6b27d6428451db6'),
('Fishes live in the sea, as men do a-land the great ones eat up the little ones.','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['great','men','nature']::text[],'d6e362b16e3eb78690c8b1388b482b4a448b59aa'),
('Lord, Lord, how subject we old men are to this vice of lying!','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['men']::text[],'aaeddc9d85088eb91746a641a13a246f933bfb21'),
('Women may fall when there''s no strength in men.','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['men','strength','women']::text[],'f79bee25763e0f1586cc40d282a2117ca25ebf35'),
('If we are marked to die, we are enough to do our country loss and if to live, the fewer men, the greater share of honor.','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['men']::text[],'e005ff1c50b06b50295b9364b3b58a2d3ed115e7'),
('Faith, there hath been many great men that have flattered the people who ne''er loved them.','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['faith','great','men']::text[],'4e9dca3c8373e227ee3f578dcd8ece6647879439'),
('Time and the hour run through the roughest day.','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['time']::text[],'8eafff89e4df37019578c4a84894fe0d098774ad'),
('It is not in the stars to hold our destiny but in ourselves.','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['future']::text[],'9e619557b86ccaf77e8d09649412bfe6faa3c018'),
('Talking isn''t doing. It is a kind of good deed to say well and yet words are not deeds.','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['good']::text[],'e0776b8368ad66ff730363042213b67fea0a667e'),
('All the world''s a stage, and all the men and women merely players: they have their exits and their entrances and one man in his time plays many parts, his acts being seven ages.','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['men','time','women']::text[],'82dfe8998ea32cfeaf0f564e93abf5b97a209e01'),
('Some are born great, some achieve greatness, and some have greatness thrust upon them.','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['great']::text[],'8edcf7f74034534a78d5c24826873faff27e8a89'),
('Our peace shall stand as firm as rocky mountains.','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['peace']::text[],'5f61f2a43ca55efc8630e699a123977b2bb973a8'),
('How poor are they that have not patience! What wound did ever heal but by degrees?','William Shakespeare',ARRAY['patience']::text[],'ecf8cd19b8c660a3644e0c1c3efeb9f973726f24'),
('I love technology.','William Shatner',ARRAY['technology']::text[],'6c83d6c4f248a19a45152721a76ff0a241a2beb3'),
('I think of doing a series as very hard work. But then I''ve talked to coal miners, and that''s really hard work.','William Shatner',ARRAY['work']::text[],'b915ba5ecd9b49dcd688c6480c34e85ce1d49cc5'),
('I love the concept of togetherness and the entwinement of marriage.','William Shatner',ARRAY['marriage']::text[],'f604b0ae35073470d820ecccc7e8c254256b3783'),
('My dad was good with actions.','William Shatner',ARRAY['dad']::text[],'d13ea9339371d7162a302920c7e88294e06b8f62'),
('No, I don''t regret anything at this point. That may change on the next phone call, but at the moment I don''t regret anything.','William Shatner',ARRAY['change']::text[],'3b2aed035e18e9ebd3c316ba0d5cd280c173a0d2'),
('My dad died of a stroke.','William Shatner',ARRAY['dad']::text[],'5738f3757988f7304793a5ba2c484c2e4fc74383'),
('You need to be silly to be funny.','William Shatner',ARRAY['funny']::text[],'b801f37c116c9e9a1fcbede129d08f934e0a9506'),
('Every piece of entertainment is made with the idea that ''This is going to be terrific'' and ''This is the best thing I''ve ever done'' and then it hits the public and then the public tells you whether it''s good or bad.','William Shatner',ARRAY['best']::text[],'2f308e6b3c94e6e3988d51d4e45f08002b0429fb'),
('Well-written words are music.','William Shatner',ARRAY['music']::text[],'7744b5357a39629705127cfa8b95c4e070c6b2c3'),
('Death is an absolute marvel.','William Shatner',ARRAY['death']::text[],'c9d9983e9568d2b8777d25518143f81b3dd77f62'),
('If saving money is wrong, I don''t want to be right!','William Shatner',ARRAY['money']::text[],'9015d666700ec835d1ef0b7420085905a7d40b74'),
('Divorce is probably as painful as death.','William Shatner',ARRAY['death']::text[],'5f93f4d3c217ac68c6a3135a039f424f75dcc194'),
('But if you want to know the truth, the weirdest thing that has happened has been my discovery that people who attend the conventions are filled with love.','William Shatner',ARRAY['truth']::text[],'fd4d2e6599e4ca5dd182a8fd66197bf8f141d600'),
('You and I and everybody in show business and the entertainment industry fly by the seat of our pants. We don''t know quite what is going to happen.','William Shatner',ARRAY['business']::text[],'985fb047ca3f00d07956cbdc805d9cbf00539692'),
('Although I''m a business major out of McGill University, I know nothing... but then I found out much later in life, nobody knows anything.','William Shatner',ARRAY['business']::text[],'54b5f39c25358c47c05f1b5ac96b7681b09edfce'),
('When I did the film Generations, in which the character died, I felt like a guest for the first time. That made me very sad.','William Shatner',ARRAY['sad']::text[],'a7fe5e0cacd119496db8ac4b312c1455dadba914'),
('Nature is perfect.','William Shatner',ARRAY['nature']::text[],'46dc39a2dac90d0c88e17a26ed88898be970fd45'),
('The mysteriousness and mystique of space is such, that science fiction attempts to tantalize you by telling you a story that could possibly be out there and that''s the appeal of science fiction.','William Shatner',ARRAY['science']::text[],'52659afaf6a1d0dc95f84fcfaea38313166ac1f7'),
('How do I stay so healthy and boyishly handsome? It''s simple. I drink the blood of young runaways.','William Shatner',ARRAY['health']::text[],'4b2c184e69649c2aeed9565073edea06751f30eb'),
('The possibilities that are suggested in quantum physics tell us that everything that we''re looking at may not be in fact there, so the underlying nature of being is weird.','William Shatner',ARRAY['nature']::text[],'75bf2fc57c9ba38489ad005a655bb5744cbdaab7'),
('We live in grief for having left the womb, for having left the teat, then school, then home. In my case, it was leaving marriages, and the death of my wife.','William Shatner',ARRAY['death','home']::text[],'f87cd12c00e7b0ca4b336d40662d8d99583a14cb'),
('Writing is truly a creative art - putting word to a blank piece of paper and ending up with a full-fledged story rife with character and plot.','William Shatner',ARRAY['art']::text[],'5957377bb5441256684bcd28f3148b36745c58b8'),
('I don''t know how I got to this point but it must be as a result of everything that has come before so if I were to change something, I might not be at this point now.','William Shatner',ARRAY['change']::text[],'ff91c5354f66a346d028b80941649405c02f1857'),
('Success should always be just beyond your grasp.','William Shatner',ARRAY['success']::text[],'3fab36c39cbbc9b10fd293a5aec37c7156060239'),
('There''s a joy and a pain about directing where the dreams you have are becoming concrete but the attention to detail, the need for time is such that it''s overwhelming at times, and the stream of responsibility.','William Shatner',ARRAY['dreams']::text[],'ec5e62eda030e6736793391263d1986a90ac4e76'),
('My kids say if there''s any family dinner that doesn''t result in somebody crying, it''s not a good dinner. They cry because it helps relieve them of a guilt or some onerous emotional burden. It''s like a family tradition.','William Shatner',ARRAY['family']::text[],'2395c8b786638860cc3332a73d7c8ab9dc32d346'),
('Sci-fi films are the epic films of the day because we can no longer put 10,000 extras in the scene - but we can draw thousands of aliens with computers.','William Shatner',ARRAY['computers']::text[],'e677b5016d15b77c2dd12e999ed651cae97123e0'),
('Hope is a flatterer, but the most upright of all parasites for she frequents the poor man''s hut, as well as the palace of his superior.','William Shenstone',ARRAY['hope']::text[],'5296f6434d3d48ff1daf52f7fc2656f8782aef35'),
('His knowledge of books had in some degree diminished his knowledge of the world.','William Shenstone',ARRAY['knowledge']::text[],'be4ef12e7e79d39aecd1f3aaddba162a30dcd474'),
('Poetry and consumption are the most flattering of diseases.','William Shenstone',ARRAY['poetry']::text[],'3d043e254dd7b16d9a7e6f4fd5c177978ef68b4c'),
('The best time to frame an answer to the letters of a friend, is the moment you receive them. Then the warmth of friendship, and the intelligence received, most forcibly cooperate.','William Shenstone',ARRAY['friendship','intelligence']::text[],'3ff101723b2325ac420d533485343836ae290316'),
('Anger is a great force. If you control it, it can be transmuted into a power which can move the whole world.','William Shenstone',ARRAY['anger']::text[],'3a679d59905cf63f51b97b276b8367c664ba2724'),
('Grandeur and beauty are so very opposite, that you often diminish the one as you increase the other. Variety is most akin to the latter, simplicity to the former.','William Shenstone',ARRAY['beauty']::text[],'3f583d150d04cbd585210cb57365512f031eddc7'),
('A liar begins with making falsehood appear like truth, and ends with making truth itself appear like falsehood.','William Shenstone',ARRAY['truth']::text[],'782c552444b7523702946581904a2ae46128cff4'),
('Zealous men are ever displaying to you the strength of their belief, while judicious men are showing you the grounds of it.','William Shenstone',ARRAY['strength']::text[],'a1a98abf7475ef8d07a761157ec1fb1c7ec32618'),
('Laws are generally found to be nets of such a texture, as the little creep through, the great break through, and the middle-sized are alone entangled in it.','William Shenstone',ARRAY['alone']::text[],'f507803572223ce62e8ce829197d9c97d5dc640f'),
('The lines of poetry, the period of prose, and even the texts of Scripture most frequently recollected and quoted, are those which are felt to be preeminently musical.','William Shenstone',ARRAY['poetry']::text[],'e880c0f9c1767ecac3d2e6efe1675250b9e0a8e1'),
('Jealousy is the fear or apprehension of superiority: envy our uneasiness under it.','William Shenstone',ARRAY['fear','jealousy']::text[],'6b4a6dd7e4021097da06dd046d3f07f35084b310'),
('The proper means of increasing the love we bear our native country is to reside some time in a foreign one.','William Shenstone',ARRAY['patriotism']::text[],'14ae6e732709adcc3d426789f9ee5fd1f435ed71'),
('Words alone cannot fully convey the realities of the soul or the greatness of the human spirit.','William Shirley',ARRAY['alone']::text[],'2d2a580ba62159873d82478dd170c755f2d48ed0'),
('Mysteriously and in ways that are totally remote from natural experience, the gray drizzle of horror induced by depression takes on the quality of physical pain.','William Styron',ARRAY['experience']::text[],'0e7ecd5d3eb86c6dd616931e2b160218a0bfd469'),
('Reading - the best state yet to keep absolute loneliness at bay.','William Styron',ARRAY['best']::text[],'7fb67ad124c26829fd1d394ad8676af59d11f940'),
('In our Country... one class of men makes war and leaves another to fight it out.','William Tecumseh Sherman',ARRAY['war']::text[],'3da2c94324c12c0431ab59e1995af251497bd997'),
('Every attempt to make war easy and safe will result in humiliation and disaster.','William Tecumseh Sherman',ARRAY['war']::text[],'d143504f7d22deadc845ecc2a20345ac07941c62'),
('War is at its best barbarism.','William Tecumseh Sherman',ARRAY['war']::text[],'64eae5958315715aa1e558b773ea103a0c6f99b5'),
('Courage - a perfect sensibility of the measure of danger, and a mental willingness to endure it.','William Tecumseh Sherman',ARRAY['courage']::text[],'55882f1ae0f1101771f2b87d913e42d850b76ab1'),
('I know I had no hand in making this war, and I know I will make more sacrifices today than any of you to secure peace.','William Tecumseh Sherman',ARRAY['peace','war']::text[],'9ccf2f70280ee98621cd64ecd1d68506a2962cc5'),
('War is cruelty. There is no use trying to reform it. The crueler it is, the sooner it will be over.','William Tecumseh Sherman',ARRAY['war']::text[],'05d6621e66276ac6a9a9a9d2274eeac240491f49'),
('I hate newspapermen. They come into camp and pick up their camp rumors and print them as facts. I regard them as spies, which, in truth, they are.','William Tecumseh Sherman',ARRAY['truth']::text[],'bc74d92769f1bbd2024cefc37b3f97468c5b1d79'),
('If the people raise a great howl against my barbarity and cruelty, I will answer that war is war, and not popularity seeking.','William Tecumseh Sherman',ARRAY['war']::text[],'d7c4293145729ef98bf4fcfb0703cf6eec986958'),
('There''s many a boy here today who looks on war as all glory but it is all hell.','William Tecumseh Sherman',ARRAY['war']::text[],'fe975e474ad0876f6d3211792c231f471b8f7485'),
('War is the remedy that our enemies have chosen, and I say let us give them all they want.','William Tecumseh Sherman',ARRAY['war']::text[],'8148379831da15aaa0fa4652c562c0102bb490cc'),
('But, my dear sirs, when peace does come, you may call on me for any thing. Then will I share with you the last cracker, and watch with you to shield your homes and families against danger from every quarter.','William Tecumseh Sherman',ARRAY['peace']::text[],'6e944a5ee099c5e7c5111edd40818abd127706b2'),
('War is too serious a matter to leave to soldiers.','William Tecumseh Sherman',ARRAY['war']::text[],'3bd51c59e658efe520bc8e776f4eb21c6956710a'),
('This war differs from other wars, in this particular. We are not fighting armies but a hostile people, and must make old and young, rich and poor, feel the hard hand of war.','William Tecumseh Sherman',ARRAY['war']::text[],'6c4ab544ddc4e75d7b2b0b95dd2cb9fd98e61d37'),
('If nominated, I will not run if elected, I will not serve.','William Tecumseh Sherman',ARRAY['politics']::text[],'ce17375dbcd55a2e8eb799c566b32c4287dd3b92'),
('My aim, then, was to whip the rebels, to humble their pride, to follow them to their inmost recesses, and make them fear and dread us. Fear is the beginning of wisdom.','William Tecumseh Sherman',ARRAY['fear','wisdom']::text[],'1af7e1edb274ab65fd5caa66e5beb39f01312885'),
('My aim then was to whip the rebels, to humble their pride, to follow them to their inmost recesses, and make them fear and dread us.','William Tecumseh Sherman',ARRAY['fear']::text[],'3f93bce4580b65302379773e679d9c224ad7f85c'),
('He belonged to that army known as invincible in peace, invisible in war.','William Tecumseh Sherman',ARRAY['peace','war']::text[],'ea7f7df0d0be87a1fad6683b95a82a4d31ad4672'),
('I am tired and sick of war. Its glory is all moonshine. It is only those who have neither fired a shot nor heard the shrieks and groans of the wounded who cry aloud for blood, for vengeance, for desolation. War is hell.','William Tecumseh Sherman',ARRAY['war']::text[],'7f060d51d1eb1d11f1b9a292dde51fbc96551e08'),
('There is many a boy here today who looks on war as all glory, but, boys, it is all hell.','William Tecumseh Sherman',ARRAY['war']::text[],'59dd6eaf1be27354e522f35c3e054c2874626b80'),
('An Army is a collection of armed men obliged to obey one man. Every change in the rules which impairs the principle weakens the army.','William Tecumseh Sherman',ARRAY['change']::text[],'1ccdc47f43f2040a16ef705478a19f73ee56306a'),
('I would make this war as severe as possible, and show no symptoms of tiring till the South begs for mercy.','William Tecumseh Sherman',ARRAY['war']::text[],'f74cc469f183c0a4d4f411967d88f61357f9b122'),
('It is only those who have neither fired a shot nor heard the shrieks and groans of the wounded who cry aloud for blood, more vengeance, more desolation. War is hell.','William Tecumseh Sherman',ARRAY['war']::text[],'14a6bd56744201f484f38bfbdb641d8254f35765'),
('You cannot qualify war in harsher terms than I will.','William Tecumseh Sherman',ARRAY['war']::text[],'5bf1262771081e8ee6e67e32485510f72aa30ed5'),
('The scenes on this field would have cured anybody of war.','William Tecumseh Sherman',ARRAY['war']::text[],'87ece46a0234416b879217f9922ff38ec012063c'),
('I beg to present you as a Christmas gift the city of Savannah.','William Tecumseh Sherman',ARRAY['christmas']::text[],'7d33c918fe69b8abd1da8f5b681aba5ffc854f08'),
('The capacity you''re thinking of is imagination without it there can be no understanding, indeed no fiction.','William Trevor',ARRAY['imagination']::text[],'b2e3e5bfb349607ffb064e32f5ee76dbde07efcf'),
('My overcoat is worn out my shirts also are worn out. And I ask to be allowed to have a lamp in the evening it is indeed wearisome sitting alone in the dark.','William Tyndale',ARRAY['alone']::text[],'ecf3b7bceafea4188526bf85f7fd69c6ac6d5626'),
('To see how Christ was prophesied and described therein, consider and mark, how that the kid or lamb must be with out spot or blemish and so was Christ only of all mankind, in the sight of God and of his law.','William Tyndale',ARRAY['easter']::text[],'3726976c59ef070f7c7498285457fb85a9a24035'),
('I perceived how that it was impossible to establish the lay people in any truth except the Scripture were plainly laid before their eyes in their mother tongue.','William Tyndale',ARRAY['truth']::text[],'ed1550279f2f31724e55ff9d60660eb2421463f9'),
('Every man dies. Not every man really lives.','William Wallace',ARRAY['life']::text[],'bf990e08704474c1f19993bee016602ac2a7ef7d'),
('Enthusiasm is that temper of the mind in which the imagination has got the better of the judgment.','William Warburton',ARRAY['imagination']::text[],'94ddf583116823755b8d0ff39ce3be73d7a59b5f'),
('People don''t follow titles, they follow courage.','William Wells Brown',ARRAY['courage']::text[],'b159ec34f4e6abf19287571abc3ef5fcec241d1f'),
('When I took command in Vietnam, I gave great emphasis to food and medical care - and to the mail.','William Westmoreland',ARRAY['food','medical']::text[],'28b9230318054312fd149975cbb72b060fc36b05'),
('War is fear cloaked in courage.','William Westmoreland',ARRAY['courage','fear','war']::text[],'b9eb30a961e25aa20473662d3a454176b3d292d9'),
('We had the best food any battlefield ever had.','William Westmoreland',ARRAY['food']::text[],'da6293ebef81fd1f4ee57574b1a264d68ac06648'),
('The military don''t start wars. Politicians start wars.','William Westmoreland',ARRAY['war']::text[],'5d75dcc7f44557adac0b4c5cd5deead61acd000e'),
('President Johnson did not want the Vietnam War to broaden. He wanted the North Vietnamese to leave their brothers in the South alone.','William Westmoreland',ARRAY['alone']::text[],'63cfe6537e0871fbf6b71578c66562dbfa4ae1e1'),
('I do not believe that the men who served in uniform in Vietnam have been given the credit they deserve. It was a difficult war against an unorthodox enemy.','William Westmoreland',ARRAY['war']::text[],'72997b40fdf4423843bc37fe044014095f2c0504'),
('We were succeeding. When you looked at specifics, this became a war of attrition. We were winning.','William Westmoreland',ARRAY['war']::text[],'f888c20f8be02e8e74be83b397233cb9bea1f9c3'),
('Every failure is a step to success.','William Whewell',ARRAY['failure','success']::text[],'257bec565814b409379f9338ca2b499f8aa23221'),
('With an eye made quiet by the power of harmony, and the deep power of joy, we see into the life of things.','William Wordsworth',ARRAY['life','power']::text[],'fbcb53f21ecf6f193b54a39a7a83e93b840f2e4d'),
('Wisdom is oftentimes nearer when we stoop than when we soar.','William Wordsworth',ARRAY['wisdom']::text[],'2b5def74254ba5ca3b0571947bffb9c8f1a804bf'),
('Golf is a day spent in a round of strenuous idleness.','William Wordsworth',ARRAY['sports']::text[],'fb4537a4013395ed4faa60524fb7668a9a980d0c'),
('Poetry is the spontaneous overflow of powerful feelings: it takes its origin from emotion recollected in tranquility.','William Wordsworth',ARRAY['poetry']::text[],'25eecee953b2e70ba1632bbb7728dd10ebe707b4'),
('That best portion of a man''s life, his little, nameless, unremembered acts of kindness and love.','William Wordsworth',ARRAY['best']::text[],'ec874a4562c363c7fd31ff7af7d99aa5365c45a8'),
('Nature never did betray the heart that loved her.','William Wordsworth',ARRAY['nature']::text[],'5dc64cc1b3361aba5318ec07f7770d3681b0a828'),
('I listened, motionless and still And, as I mounted up the hill, The music in my heart I bore, Long after it was heard no more.','William Wordsworth',ARRAY['music']::text[],'baa32d0755503fd64a6666c7fd28746072f79518'),
('The world is too much with us late and soon, getting and spending, we lay waste our powers: Little we see in Nature that is ours.','William Wordsworth',ARRAY['nature']::text[],'c8c18d10ba1d5a2879ebb447a5d5d2c5fde675da'),
('Suffering is permanent, obscure and dark, And shares the nature of infinity.','William Wordsworth',ARRAY['nature']::text[],'ff006e6122bcb3115979d0e73ef5c13f81c3b38d'),
('Come forth into the light of things, let nature be your teacher.','William Wordsworth',ARRAY['nature','teacher']::text[],'363e3bc213aa44e2f3594631b1ac3d72dd8236e3'),
('The mind that is wise mourns less for what age takes away than what it leaves behind.','William Wordsworth',ARRAY['age']::text[],'c573a8f1a927f7061e0770f41f12f03fb5e2724c'),
('Not without hope we suffer and we mourn.','William Wordsworth',ARRAY['hope']::text[],'7f147dfbbc90cad9624e3755e3ad5123cd7f0750'),
('In modern business it is not the crook who is to be feared most, it is the honest man who doesn''t know what he is doing.','William Wordsworth',ARRAY['business']::text[],'1a185dfde7f6f4a541e950d3a68160dd91d575e8'),
('For I have learned to look on nature, not as in the hour of thoughtless youth, but hearing oftentimes the still, sad music of humanity.','William Wordsworth',ARRAY['music','nature','sad']::text[],'1695b4f1cd66c072808729394933c4a3825caaaa'),
('Getting and spending, we lay waste our powers.','William Wordsworth',ARRAY['power']::text[],'d1f48d25b8ec2c0bbed7d61a3d9ae7b2eaeafc6e'),
('Pictures deface walls more often than they decorate them.','William Wordsworth',ARRAY['art']::text[],'a0ae79d85ce868a0664eedfb58a53ec4441e3a36'),
('When from our better selves we have too long been parted by the hurrying world, and droop. Sick of its business, of its pleasures tired, how gracious, how benign is solitude.','William Wordsworth',ARRAY['business']::text[],'7f4b4409bd6e9994ea161740f370918fd5b3d8bc'),
('How does the Meadow flower its bloom unfold? Because the lovely little flower is free down to its root, and in that freedom bold.','William Wordsworth',ARRAY['freedom']::text[],'05f5f8f7464a0b6df09cbf375759f0ab21df10e8'),
('The child is father of the man.','William Wordsworth',ARRAY['dad']::text[],'65d4892805fc76badd0caf3b544d9d646e541402'),
('But an old age serene and bright, and lovely as a Lapland night, shall lead thee to thy grave.','William Wordsworth',ARRAY['age']::text[],'4eb43d761e7ba1e5af20fa85e131ea71bb92d14b'),
('Life is divided into three terms - that which was, which is, and which will be. Let us learn from the past to profit by the present, and from the present, to live better in the future.','William Wordsworth',ARRAY['future','life']::text[],'f657da7cb71b9baaacceb915033ff25833419da5'),
('The human mind is capable of excitement without the application of gross and violent stimulants and he must have a very faint perception of its beauty and dignity who does not know this.','William Wordsworth',ARRAY['beauty']::text[],'5c419e869881bef041a2cc9dc99a584fccff31f4'),
('Faith is a passionate intuition.','William Wordsworth',ARRAY['faith']::text[],'9d935ad92cba730df30792b3f6ff0e087288b497'),
('The best portion of a good man''s life is his little, nameless, unremembered acts of kindness and of love.','William Wordsworth',ARRAY['best','good']::text[],'909caa42d89183e0d4027a77723193d6517ea52f'),
('Good fellowship and friendship are lasting, rational and manly pleasures.','William Wycherley',ARRAY['friendship']::text[],'087845a036767f7d44afedf2d05b5efdc2c6270b'),
('Hunger, revenge, to sleep are petty foes, But only death the jealous eyes can close.','William Wycherley',ARRAY['death','jealousy']::text[],'cd41924fa0996202252442a77fbb40185961a414'),
('Wit is more necessary than beauty and I think no young woman ugly that has it, and no handsome woman agreeable without it.','William Wycherley',ARRAY['beauty']::text[],'c23d240b5eb336a5a1dc2dd1fba98657c9e2d8dd'),
('It''s a miserable life in Hollywood. You''re up at five or six o''clock in the morning to be ready to start shooting at nine.','William Wyler',ARRAY['morning']::text[],'ec83f5da94e28408e5e27afc07435dd6ae5b49df'),
('At ten I was playing against 18-year-old guys. At 15 I was playing professional ball with the Birmingham Black Barons, so I really came very quickly in all sports.','Willie Mays',ARRAY['sports']::text[],'2806b0d6526efd8c881f64a3652b27fd560dbb1a'),
('I was very fortunate to play sports. All the anger in me went out. I had to do what I had to do. If you stay angry all the time, then you really don''t have a good life.','Willie Mays',ARRAY['anger','sports']::text[],'6f58876057f99a6793d0474366abed580c1940a8'),
('Baseball is a game, yes. It is also a business. But what is most truly is is disguised combat. For all its gentility, its almost leisurely pace, baseball is violence under wraps.','Willie Mays',ARRAY['business']::text[],'edd3974570380060f83ba5c8ddf35b107bf6d4a1'),
('That''s how easy baseball was for me. I''m not trying to brag or anything, but I had the knowledge before I became a professional baseball player to do all these things and know what each guy would hit.','Willie Mays',ARRAY['knowledge']::text[],'ccf2c2c84cb9e8f95c863abf1db8791fcb58f565'),
('His claim to his home is deep, but there are too many ghosts. He must absorb without being absorbed.','Willie Morris',ARRAY['home']::text[],'22bfe3655d4e8afae31a0fe01435d9a01c1015bf'),
('I don''t think any person has any special knowledge about what God has planned for me and you any more than me and you do.','Willie Nelson',ARRAY['knowledge']::text[],'15a54836f24b7ea4a602a5d40b377833acfadcb9'),
('There''s a great enthusiasm for good country music all over the world.','Willie Nelson',ARRAY['music']::text[],'f07543b8a6e30f8a9cc766fb92e0b8818a9e661a'),
('I wanted to connect all people who are thinking about peace on Earth.','Willie Nelson',ARRAY['peace']::text[],'f36eb4ad883943f8d95528d2f9b518a1adb770ba'),
('Well the country songs themselves are three-chord stories, ballads which are mostly sad. If you are already feeling sorry for yourself when you listen to them they will take you to an even sadder place.','Willie Nelson',ARRAY['sad']::text[],'ff90edd3a2a5269156652e5705ffb9d6549f152c'),
('America, to me, is freedom.','Willie Nelson',ARRAY['freedom']::text[],'5e4d8ec21d05703b267ef0a21d2947552845e5d8'),
('A lot of country music is sad.','Willie Nelson',ARRAY['music','sad']::text[],'15bbb526bd4b358d003ff0f46d0e40a7fcca5919'),
('I would like to see more airplay for all artists, no matter what age. I think there''s a lot of money being spent toward the young guys, but a lot of the older guys are the ones who blazed the trail for those young guys.','Willie Nelson',ARRAY['age','money']::text[],'e37a7cdc96f43e9c5931df00c8fb1a0a35dde9e7'),
('Once you replace negative thoughts with positive ones, you''ll start having positive results.','Willie Nelson',ARRAY['positive']::text[],'089bab2a77b330d327ca9317bc6fc7327b53bb5c'),
('Freedom is control in your own life.','Willie Nelson',ARRAY['freedom']::text[],'cabfb615afd093e5de227cf07593df62e207ac3f'),
('Three chords and the truth - that''s what a country song is.','Willie Nelson',ARRAY['truth']::text[],'0f6df5179c793dfba99937f10dde8d7749243967'),
('I think most art comes out of poverty and hard times.','Willie Nelson',ARRAY['art']::text[],'e5da3cec367b457063b4943c4d9706919dd2fbaf'),
('I''m a romantic slob!','Willie Nelson',ARRAY['romantic']::text[],'c07c9f7a3bb8d157c5dda23c349ddafc6379d1b6'),
('It doesn''t hurt to feel sad from time to time.','Willie Nelson',ARRAY['sad']::text[],'318ba3a7cda99d65357901bc39c103c02e09ee0d'),
('I never gave up on country music because I knew what I was doing was not that bad.','Willie Nelson',ARRAY['music']::text[],'6f02353d1c4eac4fb81d124583c6d1e5fe38bfad'),
('I think Ray Charles did as much as anybody when he did his country music album. Ray Charles broke down borders and showed the similarities between country music and R&ampB.','Willie Nelson',ARRAY['music']::text[],'cb746693aacb2d21d4f2e8fcb5aad2f8eb7cde1c'),
('I am not a pig farmer. The pigs had a great time, but I didn''t make any money.','Willie Nelson',ARRAY['money']::text[],'abf5f4d9ef6e5659137a33c720f97a41b07f31e5'),
('All I do is play music and golf - which one do you want me to give up?','Willie Nelson',ARRAY['music']::text[],'0b37319e5950a250f5194a3ec1a21ff7309d54f5'),
('If you got the money honey I got the time and when you run out of money honey I run out of time.','Willie Nelson',ARRAY['money']::text[],'65dc2144c4bb9cd3229bbc9dd0d237a9807214b7'),
('I think I''m basically the same guy I always was. Maybe I''ve learned, through experience, to rein in some of the anger and temper they say redheads normally have.','Willie Nelson',ARRAY['anger','experience']::text[],'e49dadfed56f1ec4f83f12e39ffd478230a03ede'),
('It often takes more courage to change one''s opinion than to keep it.','Willy Brandt',ARRAY['courage']::text[],'bbb7efc0081b6acd979b33b17740ad42cada6eb3'),
('We need the kind of leadership exemplified by President Kennedy to just do it! But we must do it as good stewards, aggressively exerting control over the moon. We can best do this by going there.','Wilson Greatbatch',ARRAY['leadership']::text[],'b1feff19e6926c705d255e77d4fc45097d13ec90'),
('When you buy a gallon of gas, over 60 percent of the energy you pay for goes out the radiator in the form of waste heat? That''s why you have a radiator in your car in the first place.','Wilson Greatbatch',ARRAY['car']::text[],'047a2b64cb90aaa8b40ad3ef1ec5e3e199d57d73'),
('Failure has gone to his head.','Wilson Mizner',ARRAY['failure']::text[],'aa907f2de40482f8295fb0ef369cb41e0bacea54'),
('The difference between chirping out of turn and a faux pas depends on what kind of a bar you''re in.','Wilson Mizner',ARRAY['wisdom']::text[],'cdbfc27e07e13d9aa40af15b9add765f3f73e380'),
('Those who welcome death have only tried it from the ears up.','Wilson Mizner',ARRAY['death']::text[],'19219eb38f5a714bfb47cc6a94c10ffe3469818b'),
('I respect faith, but doubt is what gives you an education.','Wilson Mizner',ARRAY['education','faith','respect']::text[],'65307f173ff8f51dcf7573dd81c6b06efce5a823'),
('God help those who do not help themselves.','Wilson Mizner',ARRAY['god']::text[],'8c1a1fe62962f68e5cc51b2e653100d581865ff8'),
('The best way to keep your friends is not to give them away.','Wilson Mizner',ARRAY['best']::text[],'cfd0825841c81bd89fcb480fb1624158ea623fde'),
('Art is science made clear.','Wilson Mizner',ARRAY['art','science']::text[],'0222575125da949bbd0ba158fd2bb62f213c359d'),
('To profit from good advice requires more wisdom than to give it.','Wilson Mizner',ARRAY['wisdom']::text[],'24fd3d1a01a699da95f6f617c99df1986fdb6f81'),
('The most efficient water power in the world - women''s tears.','Wilson Mizner',ARRAY['power','women']::text[],'7375549a822fd7f16fb5aa8f4b41b4f8ee068e71'),
('It is not in life, but in art that self-fulfillment is to be found.','Wilson Mizner',ARRAY['art']::text[],'eef34422abd2a14f466d7d3ea5f19ed60c5ee016'),
('And I remember leaving my place in L.A. and - my father is a big fight fan - and I said, ''Dad, I got a couple of days off and I''m getting ready to go to Houston to sign to fight Muhammad Ali.','Wilt Chamberlain',ARRAY['dad']::text[],'4291363a78ae69bc09e0e79c9fafd5eae1ed4ba1'),
('Nobody roots for Goliath.','Wilt Chamberlain',ARRAY['sports']::text[],'b309bb0f457cda117326a560d9cf5395007fa39c'),
('With all of you men out there who think that having a thousand different ladies is pretty cool, I have learned in my life I''ve found out that having one woman a thousand different times is much more satisfying.','Wilt Chamberlain',ARRAY['cool']::text[],'67d7792a963cad47c0d3a54a2559db77c2a70a25'),
('My politics are of a practical kind - the integrity of the country, the supremacy of the Federal government, an honorable peace, or none at all.','Winfield Scott Hancock',ARRAY['government','peace','politics']::text[],'7900eff6fc3dfcd5c6f2c594a50cefeb51c46680'),
('The crown of life is neither happiness nor annihilation it is understanding.','Winifred Holtby',ARRAY['happiness']::text[],'7892e4b588746515a5b662557db084cc872991b5'),
('Politics is almost as exciting as war, and quite as dangerous. In war you can only be killed once, but in politics many times.','Winston Churchill',ARRAY['politics','war']::text[],'3e02b53299595f54778ec089cb6f9718a8d2d2b6'),
('Courage is what it takes to stand up and speak courage is also what it takes to sit down and listen.','Winston Churchill',ARRAY['courage']::text[],'6d6a734ca7c8122ca17498f51f740023a8eb27d3'),
('Courage is rightly esteemed the first of human qualities... because it is the quality which guarantees all others.','Winston Churchill',ARRAY['courage']::text[],'3641d9c0ea7fa43cf0c3d561039b39a52290aae0'),
('The short words are best, and the old words are the best of all.','Winston Churchill',ARRAY['best']::text[],'6077813e80202fd018940416773008d0b23dadd1'),
('Socialism is a philosophy of failure, the creed of ignorance, and the gospel of envy, its inherent virtue is the equal sharing of misery.','Winston Churchill',ARRAY['failure']::text[],'ea1e22a1e8f6e2bf2a4e74ab2ab3177bdd29b16c'),
('Short words are best and the old words when short are best of all.','Winston Churchill',ARRAY['best']::text[],'67cf54752f5a44c53b80cc2ecbeb8b6d8a13ea6e'),
('If you''re going through hell, keep going.','Winston Churchill',ARRAY['motivational']::text[],'33cfeae8b2aaf9ed2902fea2d5860431b7227b3b'),
('If you have an important point to make, don''t try to be subtle or clever. Use a pile driver. Hit the point once. Then come back and hit it again. Then hit it a third time - a tremendous whack.','Winston Churchill',ARRAY['time']::text[],'c0e7d2ff1281ac68725853addcd6af655a6578db'),
('You have enemies? Good. That means you''ve stood up for something, sometime in your life.','Winston Churchill',ARRAY['good','life']::text[],'14dbee63aae4848c9597f2743f3f172a7b4b9f82'),
('I am easily satisfied with the very best.','Winston Churchill',ARRAY['best']::text[],'6fc9900ba703ee775373d79dc1f05c4d6d96850f'),
('You better cut the pizza in four pieces because I''m not hungry enough to eat six.','Yogi Berra',ARRAY['food']::text[],'c7e2806a3526cf3370a4a841f193b157473b7aca'),
('How can you think and hit at the same time?','Yogi Berra',ARRAY['time']::text[],'7b69c71a3e31c4875948a8214feb6d0356281731'),
('You wouldn''t have won if we''d beaten you.','Yogi Berra',ARRAY['sports']::text[],'7baba75553ec7e5113faf9afed0e95ddbed6d752'),
('A nickel ain''t worth a dime anymore.','Yogi Berra',ARRAY['funny']::text[],'99151733c1dca1a45f8b9c9e01e364aa0d2c2165'),
('The future ain''t what it used to be.','Yogi Berra',ARRAY['future']::text[],'2841a58c74c4b1c260acd49a55db53e2efd5a1c8'),
('Little League baseball is a very good thing because it keeps the parents off the streets.','Yogi Berra',ARRAY['good']::text[],'354eff091567f491ccbf5331a764fa01df5917aa'),
('I never blame myself when I''m not hitting. I just blame the bat and if it keeps up, I change bats. After all, if I know it isn''t my fault that I''m not hitting, how can I get mad at myself?','Yogi Berra',ARRAY['change']::text[],'695e03c376f0c0db870bbab6403a2151ddaf2e74'),
('Half the lies they tell about me aren''t true.','Yogi Berra',ARRAY['sports']::text[],'e5b2161f218dfaed9f0e7d85726422e73fdaf1b8'),
('I never said most of the things I said.','Yogi Berra',ARRAY['funny']::text[],'4dbad3e3137d3ebfa77d3d45018cc64dda2cad58'),
('I just go with the flow, so any style can be in my music - that makes it exciting.','Yoko Ono',ARRAY['music']::text[],'0bfbb6c8392c9a8568305ecfdb97052f0ec2b9c8'),
('If your life changes, we can change the world, too.','Yoko Ono',ARRAY['change']::text[],'4698f6048efb30860a60f8b707d7840294cd5c69'),
('When I turned 60, it didn''t bother me at all.','Yoko Ono',ARRAY['birthday']::text[],'5188ac401b39d316ce1173b5537625a06873ba9c'),
('War is over if you want it.','Yoko Ono',ARRAY['war']::text[],'6ac913803595207d466b9e80004ff085cc6a21cd'),
('Remember, each one of us has the power to change the world. Just start thinking peace, and the message will spread quicker than you think.','Yoko Ono',ARRAY['change','peace','power']::text[],'ae1dd2b02fa1dc7422f0f75d38e40d3e12609f65'),
('The nice thing about the gallery shows is that without having to pay any money you can just go and see it.','Yoko Ono',ARRAY['money']::text[],'6c90fa2ec6a78f907f20dc8bf59ccf65687a373d'),
('Is truth always positive? Of course. Once the truth comes out, you know, it''s all right. We''re scared that if the truth comes out that it''s not all right. It''s the other way around.','Yoko Ono',ARRAY['positive']::text[],'270ec2115f97513f12e96bd50ed46526ef3498f0'),
('Marriage is a gamble, let''s be honest.','Yoko Ono',ARRAY['marriage']::text[],'5e3f2e6112fe7f5b48bd4a4a638e0aaa999e1d94'),
('People make music to get a reaction. Music is communication.','Yoko Ono',ARRAY['communication']::text[],'82fc9399bb467ba771e4022f5898ca013043b2c0'),
('Countries have lost their culture because what they wanted was money. Money became the running theme in every country and culture was sacrificed.','Yoko Ono',ARRAY['money']::text[],'3f19d4231d59e6c44a66d5037dc4f1f7337369d9'),
('Controversy is part of the nature of art and creativity.','Yoko Ono',ARRAY['art','nature']::text[],'52d4770d086af6b46f87f114088be87602ca5ca3'),
('John wrote with a very deep love for the human race and a concern for its future.','Yoko Ono',ARRAY['future']::text[],'f8ef20dd30215f72b5cc7957e654db8f49aba675'),
('A dream you dream alone is only a dream. A dream you dream together is a reality.','Yoko Ono',ARRAY['alone']::text[],'f27b4d3cf606940afd0ee7f80e9c026092514603'),
('A dream you dream alone is only a dream. A dream you dream together is reality.','Yoko Ono',ARRAY['alone','dreams']::text[],'28f4361800acb2a124f936c6b325f89f0bbfdb71'),
('The 1960s were about releasing ourselves from conventional society and freeing ourselves.','Yoko Ono',ARRAY['society']::text[],'6d087c775797a9b553089eb0b58d32d07b09d5b8'),
('When I was four years old, my mother put me into a school for early music education where you get perfect pitch and harmony and composition.','Yoko Ono',ARRAY['education']::text[],'905e7725142aeabf868cae622c8ed15b67e6aab3'),
('But only art and music have the power to bring peace.','Yoko Ono',ARRAY['peace']::text[],'3ce12e9fc3dd7394f5f730936cd7a4e043783ac0'),
('Being alone is very difficult.','Yoko Ono',ARRAY['alone']::text[],'50d513d3c3067f63c47959446ea29484e9691f1e'),
('Healing yourself is connected with healing others.','Yoko Ono',ARRAY['movingon']::text[],'2876ccc1080c0c8498a3bfecd3f161d9a42d2664'),
('Smile in the mirror. Do that every morning and you''ll start to see a big difference in your life.','Yoko Ono',ARRAY['morning','smile']::text[],'ba3f877174dea937bd02c364eaa0e40911f98c1e'),
('Artists are going to be the metronome of this society.','Yoko Ono',ARRAY['society']::text[],'e85d20d5f10e86b85f9db0f737de76482fe3023b'),
('Distance doesn''t exist, in fact, and neither does time. Vibrations from love or music can be felt everywhere, at all times.','Yoko Ono',ARRAY['music']::text[],'8c363cd7ec03eb0d2dd6a88cae323492cbe90fdf'),
('I trust myself. You need that to survive.','Yoko Ono',ARRAY['trust']::text[],'2728bb7f5253484fd678a00a563174c2f146529f'),
('Events are the best teacher for us. You try to learn from people, there is always some bend to it.','Yoko Ono',ARRAY['teacher']::text[],'95bf2f03d9b830f68f22278e3b4803afd7527f8f'),
('Experiencing sadness and anger can make you feel more creative, and by being creative, you can get beyond your pain or negativity.','Yoko Ono',ARRAY['anger','sad']::text[],'a565b8a25b4df66bec24d41534f97fe1d4345942'),
('All my concerts had no sounds in them they were completely silent. People had to make up their own music in their minds!','Yoko Ono',ARRAY['music']::text[],'0992e35e5a32b982f40e807b9c34c10349d75b40'),
('When you go to war, both sides lose totally.','Yoko Ono',ARRAY['war']::text[],'a3b685e1345cecedace487ffe5e84a6de1271182'),
('The only instrument I can play is piano. Whenever I make songs at home, I play the piano and make them on the piano.','Yoko Ono',ARRAY['home']::text[],'119e990919fb9d5371416995369943b1745a7ec2'),
('What the Beatles did was something incredible, it was more than what a band could do. We have to give them respect.','Yoko Ono',ARRAY['respect']::text[],'ee06bcebbb24d4e0cc7bc68ffa238b3614703ce9'),
('Architecture is basically a container of something. I hope they will enjoy not so much the teacup, but the tea.','Yoshio Taniguchi',ARRAY['architecture','hope']::text[],'7a875b824ef654617243585c7f12f66a6b8532e2'),
('There is a brief moment when all there is in a man''s mind and soul and spirit is reflected through his eyes, his hands, his attitude. This is the moment to record.','Yousuf Karsh',ARRAY['attitude']::text[],'01b923967d5addb2cbb5a64e3fd66a3021e08779'),
('I''ve also seen that great men are often lonely. This is understandable, because they have built such high standards for themselves that they often feel alone. But that same loneliness is part of their ability to create.','Yousuf Karsh',ARRAY['alone','great','men']::text[],'5a17f4f2d78099f5c53dbf008507702407163370'),
('We need to become good citizens in the global village, instead of competing. What are we competing for - to drive more cars, eat more steaks? That will destroy the world.','Yuan T. Lee',ARRAY['car']::text[],'897486b0e23412b6bc62da64ef74197acc66dac4'),
('By means of microscopic observation and astronomical projection the lotus flower can become the foundation for an entire theory of the universe and an agent whereby we may perceive Truth.','Yukio Mishima',ARRAY['truth']::text[],'87333d1f7c190cbcfdd67bbf0207711c330903b3'),
('Girls have an unfair advantage over men: if they can''t get what they want by being smart, they can get it by being dumb.','Yul Brynner',ARRAY['men','women']::text[],'4b5032a39c79beb27af6cac89c87e181af5fc9fa'),
('A heart makes a good home for the friend.','Yunus Emre',ARRAY['home']::text[],'5a0892e00f6a40721ec2835066bbc5d5360ec4b6'),
('When the soul looks out of its body, it should see only beauty in its path. These are the sights we must hold in mind, in order to move to a higher place.','Yusef Lateef',ARRAY['beauty']::text[],'bccba5ac5bd17bb62abfa9105da709f5b133263b'),
('Everybody in their own imagination decides what scary is.','Yvonne Craig',ARRAY['imagination']::text[],'3f6a65d1b63d6f5aa4ecb31875eb37e4398f140f'),
('I need this wild life, this freedom.','Zane Grey',ARRAY['freedom']::text[],'d28a8be34c702864979e838a26156c7223cf1f84'),
('Love grows more tremendously full, swift, poignant, as the years multiply.','Zane Grey',ARRAY['anniversary']::text[],'223416642cea37e48bf54d18ac7f0d714aca9df2'),
('I hate birthdays.','Zane Grey',ARRAY['birthday']::text[],'144845ff2fd0e7112c60f42c3f353a54d68a00cf'),
('Love of man for woman - love of woman for man. That''s the nature, the meaning, the best of life itself.','Zane Grey',ARRAY['nature']::text[],'31e5c92236de3744666b45621c9c424a0a807360'),
('I arise full of eagerness and energy, knowing well what achievement lies ahead of me.','Zane Grey',ARRAY['inspirational']::text[],'d7f81a26d6682d6b4bfa3157b13843184d2ccc8e'),
('I think it is important to ask ourselves as citizens, not as Democrats attacking the administration, but as citizens, whether a world power can really provide global leadership on the basis of fear and anxiety?','Zbigniew Brzezinski',ARRAY['fear','leadership']::text[],'7d906398654db77a981fdaba211755358448d176'),
('Not to mention the fact that of course terrorists hate freedom. I think they do hate. But believe me, I don''t think they sit there abstractly hating freedom.','Zbigniew Brzezinski',ARRAY['freedom']::text[],'8cd79588733e2821b70053b5f7c5d4443b2c18f2'),
('We cannot have that relationship if we only dictate or threaten and condemn those who disagree.','Zbigniew Brzezinski',ARRAY['relationship']::text[],'e7084cbb074f36b960c1269b98a06e3648110095'),
('In Iraq we must succeed. Failure is not an option.','Zbigniew Brzezinski',ARRAY['failure']::text[],'5fde0442bfe464a6b10baa2e0652bfdd282898ac'),
('Look at Islam in a rational manner and without demagoguery or emotion. It is the leading religion of the world with 1.5 billion followers.','Zbigniew Brzezinski',ARRAY['religion']::text[],'0af93c051be9151a8410c945b96d540d7da8f4ed'),
('The first and most important is to emphasize the enduring nature of the alliance relationship particularly with Europe which does share our values and interests even if it disagrees with us on specific policies.','Zbigniew Brzezinski',ARRAY['relationship']::text[],'d0f46db195090465e6adf6f4801749645717e6e7'),
('To increase the zone of peace is to build the inner core of a stable international zone.','Zbigniew Brzezinski',ARRAY['peace']::text[],'6a2aba40842cd4fc58201bd8f44f1d27faaf4a67'),
('We have actually experienced in recent months a dramatic demonstration of an unprecedented intelligence failure, perhaps the most significant intelligence failure in the history of the United States.','Zbigniew Brzezinski',ARRAY['failure','intelligence']::text[],'db9e51f4b47bc0e650527886b3985bc5a0c58172'),
('You have already disarmed my men without my knowledge, are their arms to be returned or not?','Zebulon Pike',ARRAY['knowledge']::text[],'cc43e23ae9397db27c1a04ebb9f67900d93253f5'),
('May Heaven be propitious, and smile on the cause of my country.','Zebulon Pike',ARRAY['smile']::text[],'a7218502ff9800982d33baa24e9f999eb12a63f1'),
('Smoke the pipe of peace, bury the tomahawk, and become one nation.','Zebulon Pike',ARRAY['peace']::text[],'696b77be641950ad65127d3c96b93bcf3aefb5ac'),
('Nobody has ever measured, not even poets, how much the heart can hold.','Zelda Fitzgerald',ARRAY['love']::text[],'31ed1007ab353885ee834ad8b77368e0a6f22d42'),
('By the time a person has achieved years adequate for choosing a direction, the die is cast and the moment has long since passed which determined the future.','Zelda Fitzgerald',ARRAY['future']::text[],'17ae5eb7de034d5815a71889c931ec09986f26f9'),
('We grew up founding our dreams on the infinite promise of American advertising. I still believe that one can learn to play the piano by mail and that mud will give you a perfect complexion.','Zelda Fitzgerald',ARRAY['dreams']::text[],'38bd8772b131b406f98af824c6d9be6bfe9482fa'),
('I can remember when Democrats believed that it was the duty of America to fight for freedom over tyranny.','Zell Miller',ARRAY['freedom','politics']::text[],'ca2e45a8810f42a56abbb174d7b864f75f9eed86'),
('History can never be covered up.','Zhu Rongji',ARRAY['history']::text[],'fed48b09ae3ccfe74fd3d5db34ff99ab649142da'),
('Success is the maximum utilization of the ability that you have.','Zig Ziglar',ARRAY['success']::text[],'8f20466dfe66e3938ee05f28c0bbe31154c26670'),
('A lot of people quit looking for work as soon as they find a job.','Zig Ziglar',ARRAY['work']::text[],'617923e0d559799a60428ed24d6405365eda4ff8'),
('Money isn''t the most important thing in life, but it''s reasonably close to oxygen on the ''gotta have it'' scale.','Zig Ziglar',ARRAY['life','money']::text[],'b03c177dbce22c4869be1798dadaba07a62edea2'),
('Statistics suggest that when customers complain, business owners and managers ought to get excited about it. The complaining customer represents a huge opportunity for more business.','Zig Ziglar',ARRAY['business']::text[],'23770eabce1eba563f941572477f686e01d22b41'),
('If you can dream it, then you can achieve it. You will get all you want in life if you help enough other people get what they want.','Zig Ziglar',ARRAY['life']::text[],'dd0a37381e0fce86230704f251fcaee9d46fa343'),
('Expect the best. Prepare for the worst. Capitalize on what comes.','Zig Ziglar',ARRAY['best']::text[],'6c597be8db9b7ab21c4c8e96c8c76b889e355355'),
('Honesty and integrity are absolutely essential for success in life - all areas of life. The really good news is that anyone can develop both honesty and integrity.','Zig Ziglar',ARRAY['good','life','success']::text[],'f6edc65200308d97af4f0f2bda9e2d27452767dc'),
('The foundation stones for a balanced success are honesty, character, integrity, faith, love and loyalty.','Zig Ziglar',ARRAY['faith','love','success']::text[],'a7794a2a0a7b31e877227ba70afaa8fe06344d78'),
('You do not pay the price of success, you enjoy the price of success.','Zig Ziglar',ARRAY['success']::text[],'f657581c27caf834a186703502f77325799461a2'),
('Positive thinking will let you do everything better than negative thinking will.','Zig Ziglar',ARRAY['positive']::text[],'7bf0625ca8259f45a9858806705202c9966936dd'),
('Money won''t make you happy... but everybody wants to find out for themselves.','Zig Ziglar',ARRAY['money']::text[],'2e209ff70b6a477254bf8379b484aee236bf9d5e'),
('Success is dependent upon the glands - sweat glands.','Zig Ziglar',ARRAY['success']::text[],'838bfe283cea508202399b050f56c9aaaa7ea90a'),
('You cannot tailor-make the situations in life but you can tailor-make the attitudes to fit those situations.','Zig Ziglar',ARRAY['life']::text[],'d5bfce11d1a05a55186b8cad39d67b34728aa62c'),
('If you learn from defeat, you haven''t really lost.','Zig Ziglar',ARRAY['failure']::text[],'bcdeec3fcabb64181b4a711c91e90e64f634cea4'),
('I believe that being successful means having a balance of success stories across the many areas of your life. You can''t truly be considered successful in your business life if your home life is in shambles.','Zig Ziglar',ARRAY['business','home','life','success']::text[],'ad59f60aa7edb5d29c14b5c162ceeef285999041'),
('You can make positive deposits in your own economy every day by reading and listening to powerful, positive, life-changing content and by associating with encouraging and hope-building people.','Zig Ziglar',ARRAY['positive']::text[],'ca2143fb588e196617222ff577dea9376c468430'),
('You can have everything in life you want, if you will just help other people get what they want.','Zig Ziglar',ARRAY['life']::text[],'46393e05cc589674f1a1557a32baa02a35b65b11'),
('Little men with little minds and little imaginations go through life in little ruts, smugly resisting all changes which would jar their little worlds.','Zig Ziglar',ARRAY['life','men']::text[],'88c43695199b9ed2a8a4190df2d8a1e00ec61123'),
('Your attitude, not your aptitude, will determine your altitude.','Zig Ziglar',ARRAY['attitude']::text[],'80b3784283259640e21082970162750bc5abc387'),
('People who have good relationships at home are more effective in the marketplace.','Zig Ziglar',ARRAY['good','home']::text[],'e6c132a08e840d316b04681f351b9b20a181f4bc'),
('Failure is a detour, not a dead-end street.','Zig Ziglar',ARRAY['failure']::text[],'190fdd2348ca74db2ca541608fab9193d462f072'),
('If God would have wanted us to live in a permissive society He would have given us Ten Suggestions and not Ten Commandments.','Zig Ziglar',ARRAY['god','society']::text[],'1bb5380d06f51e55ebbbe6a58f396b7b267c4f40'),
('You cannot climb the ladder of success dressed in the costume of failure.','Zig Ziglar',ARRAY['failure','success']::text[],'b975bd8e67dd25724b1c143a8ef533491735842e'),
('Remember that failure is an event, not a person.','Zig Ziglar',ARRAY['failure']::text[],'97787fbe58f7fbccfa10e5ab2224fa651f044009'),
('When you are tough on yourself, life is going to be infinitely easier on you.','Zig Ziglar',ARRAY['life']::text[],'eba50e75b1ebeb8a061a52c0cc4c10220794d3ba'),
('I don''t know a better preparation for life than a love of poetry and a good digestion.','Zona Gale',ARRAY['poetry']::text[],'d3fa0e3862d979a26d1090cb107e6e53d25ef07e'),
('Love makes your soul crawl out from its hiding place.','Zora Neale Hurston',ARRAY['love']::text[],'5ccdc170475ce1c069ce2b72c120d9cc12fdcf9f'),
('So the brother in black offers to these United States the source of courage that endures, and laughter.','Zora Neale Hurston',ARRAY['courage']::text[],'6137fc505a3bc2a8b7bb7759e4847c7aeddc4b9a'),
('It is one of the blessings of this world that few people see visions and dream dreams.','Zora Neale Hurston',ARRAY['dreams']::text[],'9a68293b3d7f3a77f4f5be13c7dc8681b7ed5ed0'),
('There is something about poverty that smells like death.','Zora Neale Hurston',ARRAY['death']::text[],'4c47e977dced71851ec73512e71e180467dfd147'),
('The man who interprets Nature is always held in great honor.','Zora Neale Hurston',ARRAY['nature']::text[],'6576eb3149fa1dd98b6aef979a1586a3a47cceec'),
('It would be against all nature for all the Negroes to be either at the bottom, top, or in between. We will go where the internal drive carries us like everybody else. It is up to the individual.','Zora Neale Hurston',ARRAY['nature']::text[],'1a8d4a36883c3f2cc18053eda385039a31e9825b'),
('It seems to me that trying to live without friends is like milking a bear to get cream for your morning coffee. It is a whole lot of trouble, and then not worth much after you get it.','Zora Neale Hurston',ARRAY['friendship','morning']::text[],'ace23722580befdd2ff65b6a64052032bf041651'),
('Trees and plants always look like the people they live with, somehow.','Zora Neale Hurston',ARRAY['gardening']::text[],'4c0c0537e674765748a3a3d9153a8d7f913439be')
INSERT INTO quotes_library (quote, author, tags, quote_hash) VALUES
('I did not just fall in love. I made a parachute jump.','Zora Neale Hurston',ARRAY['love']::text[],'87ac08b778ccf092827bed8a984a9ed27ae4a988'),
('It''s a funny thing, the less people have to live for, the less nerve they have to risk losing nothing.','Zora Neale Hurston',ARRAY['funny']::text[],'00620f643148ae3ea074363dd4cc7959c7e40fdb'),
('The present was an egg laid by the past that had the future inside its shell.','Zora Neale Hurston',ARRAY['future']::text[],'c8e0834f30b9e9852ff13bad2fa324a63e337bea'),
('If you want that good feeling that comes from doing things for other folks then you have to pay for it in abuse and misunderstanding.','Zora Neale Hurston',ARRAY['good']::text[],'facafba197bb1d5ed4c96c2af98e7e082817ad81'),
('A thing is mighty big when time and distance cannot shrink it.','Zora Neale Hurston',ARRAY['time']::text[],'e7e29b7d2872b0c14b3651d46fd2fa683d6571ab'),
('Grab the broom of anger and drive off the beast of fear.','Zora Neale Hurston',ARRAY['anger','fear']::text[],'318a2cf437bae295c332f1c4d14de508e5d20409'),
('I want a man who''s kind and understanding. Is that too much to ask of a millionaire?','Zsa Zsa Gabor',ARRAY['valentinesday']::text[],'00850f5d1e23d8bfaf7a3756ebe9011645c5ca2c'),
('When I''m alone, I can sleep crossways in bed without an argument.','Zsa Zsa Gabor',ARRAY['alone']::text[],'1f97d49f31491a319afe6974e65fb367f17d006c'),
('The women''s movement hasn''t changed my sex life. It wouldn''t dare.','Zsa Zsa Gabor',ARRAY['women']::text[],'058a13ef9b32d951e1c5bdee26b99be01c83b5ec'),
('Getting divorced just because you don''t love a man is almost as silly as getting married just because you do.','Zsa Zsa Gabor',ARRAY['love','marriage']::text[],'ee2a228d9f8ac52d9a6d64cf2dbf131d5c5c8ed9'),
('To be loved is a strength. To love is a weakness.','Zsa Zsa Gabor',ARRAY['strength']::text[],'fedc87b8b82df0e8ffe6a0ed5740ca99d28cfbed'),
('He taught me housekeeping when I divorce I keep the house.','Zsa Zsa Gabor',ARRAY['funny']::text[],'e2ff0cfa181ffbd2378c11f2a066d8ad4b43ea18'),
('A man in love is incomplete until he has married. Then he''s finished.','Zsa Zsa Gabor',ARRAY['love','marriage']::text[],'e8641155579dc17b3426a95e5e49426cf4c7f080'),
('One of my theories is that men love with their eyes women love with their ears.','Zsa Zsa Gabor',ARRAY['women']::text[],'6121ef4b16c880481d59bca95c426695a364f300')
INSERT INTO admin_commands (type, text)
